{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-\u2bce-the-echo-chamber-\u2bce-2e-actual-play","id":1554737,"title":"\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce [2e Actual Play]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-28T12:23:06-07:00","id":1554737,"title":"\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce [2e Actual Play]","content":"<div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1540\" height=\"570\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9GgA01q.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9GgA01q.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9GgA01q.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> Here I lie<br /> In place that I can't feel<br /> Now can't I try to hold on to what is real<br /> Now it all seems to get underneath my skin<br /> Fighting for something to change in me<br /> All of this time in a panic room<br /> But nothing will make me feel safe<br /> <br /> Inside my mind<br /> I'm facing this torment<br /> Was I designed<br /> (To finally go cold)<br /> Barely alive when I was discarded<br /> So are you blind<br /> (To how you make me feel)<br /> God knows if I'll be fine<br /> God knows if I'll make it out alive<br /> You all assumed that'd be alright<br /> When I'm stuck in this <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">echo chamber</span><br /> <br /> - <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\"><i>Echo Chamber</i></span>, Defects</div> <br /> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce</span> </span></b></b><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><u>I</u>NTRODUCTIO<u>N</u></span></b></div> <br /> \u200b<br /> Hello, all, and welcome to my Actual Play! I'm a newcomer to Mage, having discovered the game a few months ago after randomly stumbling upon Ascension. I was immediately hooked by the freeform magic, the simplicity and richness of the Storytelling System, and the evocative fiction. Some of my favorite pieces of media were listed as inspirations, and a lot of the lore shared elements with a world me and some friends had built collaboratively around 10 years ago. DaveB's fantastic writeups only made the obsession worse.<br /> <br /> I had to try it out for myself. It wasn't long before I got into two weekly games, which I've been enjoying immensely. But still, something was missing\u2026 Don't get me wrong, I love me a tabletop game. But there's nothing like being on the other side of the screen, crafting a world, and watching the pure alchemy that happens when you drop a group of players right into the midst of things and see the chaos that ensues. I used to GM Pathfinder and D&amp;D, and even worked as a professional DM for some time. Some of my good friends mentioned having a free day and being open to playing something. The signs all pointed to me running a game. I just needed to figure out what kind of game I wanted to run.<br /> <br /> I'm the kind of person who doesn't do things by half measures, so I immediately got my hands on every book I could, both 1e and 2e. And the more I read, the more ideas began to percolate. When I saw the description of the Los Angeles setting (where I happen to live in real life), I knew I had to use it. But for me, a lot of the fun of Mage is in exploring the contrast between Sleeper life and Mage life, especially at the start. The seemingly endless potential, taking first steps as a mage, navigating the Orders, and the &quot;street level&quot; stuff. I think it's a shame that most games start using the standard template, skipping past all that juicy exploratory content. As I thought about that, a most devious idea blossomed in my mind.<br /> <br /> What if I kept the entire premise of the game a secret from them? None of them have read the books or know much about the game, and I wasn't about to force them to binge the books like I had. This would be the one and only opportunity to experience the world of Mage for the first time, just like their characters. So I decided I'd keep them in the dark. I told them we were playing an investigative horror game, gave them some character-building questions, and a prompt. And that's it.<br /> <br /> Here's the character building advice I gave, for those interested:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce</span> <u>T</u>HE CAS<u>T</u> | Who exactly are you?</b><br /> \u200b</span></div> \u2bcc You are in Los Angeles, a beautiful, bustling, horrifying metropolis. It's August 2025.<br /> \u2bcc Whether you're a shut-in conspiracy theorist, a politician with aspirations for the Oval Office, or the current hottest TikTok Influencer, you've got dreams of your own.<br /> \u2bcc You are about to be drawn into a series of mysteries that you can't even fathom yet.<br /> <br /> <hr />\u200b<br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\"><b>\u2bcc THINGS TO CONSIDER</b></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Genre\u200b</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Mystery / Urban Horror / Slice-of-Life / ____\u200b</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Tone\u200b</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Tragic / Tense / Slow Burn / Paranoia-Inducing\u200b</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Inspirations\u200b</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">House of Leaves / Dresden Files / Memento / Haunting of Hill House\u200b</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Themes\u200b</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Truth vs. Lies / Identity and Transformation / Echo Chambers \u200b</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <hr />\u200b<br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\"><b>\u2bcc </b>\u200b<b>ADVICE</b></span><ul><li>You can create any type of character. This is a very freeform and flexible storytelling game. Whether you're a celebrity, a grad student, a member of the FBI, or a local chef, you'll fit in the story just fine. Just make a character whose story you'll enjoy playing and exploring.\u200b</li> <li>In fact, I'd encourage you to step out of your comfort zone or go for a concept that you think is fun but that you'd normally not get to play in another system.\u200b</li> <li>Who your character is before the game starts will greatly influence the resources, knowledge, and connections you have access to. Do you want to have lots of allies and enemies? Tons of money and creature comforts? A secret life that nobody else knows about? Knowledge about a super esoteric subject? Fighting ability that would scare Bruce Lee? Build your character concept based on what you want to actually play once the story gets rolling.\u200b</li> <li>Your character needs to have a Vice that they're strongly tempted to indulge in and a Virtue that they hold dear to them. This should be a real source of conflict for them!\u200b</li> <li>They also need to be curious and interested in solving mysteries. Characters who are uninterested in the world around them probably aren't a great fit for this chronicle.\u200b</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\"><b>BIOGRAPHICAL INFO</b></span><br /> <br /> Name:<br /> Age/Birthday:<br /> Gender/Sexuality:<br /> Race/Ethnicity:<br /> Vice/Virtue:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\"><b>RELATIONSHIPS AND CONNECTIONS</b></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Who are your people? Could be biological / chosen family or not, but no man is an island.\u200b</li> <li>Who are <i>not</i> your people? Could be nuisances or enemies, but nobody is liked by everyone.\u200b</li> <li>Who do you wish was in your life? An old flame, a departed relative, a dream collaborator?\u200b</li> <li>Who have you all but forgotten? Someone who you just barely crossed paths with.\u200b</li> <li>How did you end up at the funeral?\u200b</li> </ol><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\"><b>PERSONAL QUESTIONS</b></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>What makes you feel out of place or like you don't belong?\u200b</li> <li>What's your morning routine\u2014and why do you stick to it?\u200b</li> <li>Who in your life have you disappointed? Who has disappointed you?\u200b</li> <li>What is the worst thing that's ever happened to you?\u200b</li> <li>What is something you wish someone would ask you about?\u200b</li> <li>What's a place you go back to even though it's unpleasant or painful?\u200b</li> <li>What is the worst thing you've ever done?\u200b</li> <li>What do you believe that you'd hesitate to admit to others?\u200b</li> <li>What is a weird thing that has happened to you that you don't talk about?\u200b</li> <li>What is a mystery that you NEED to solve?</li> </ol></div></div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T12:29:34-07:00","id":1554738,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce</span> <u>T</u>HE PREMIS<u>E</u></span></b></div> <br /> <div align=\"center\">\u2bcc \u2bce \u2bcc</div> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Your story starts and ends at a funeral.</span></div> <br /> <br /> You are all here for a very specific reason, even if you don't realize it at first. The simplest explanation is that you knew the deceased\u2014one of his friends, a member of the family, something like that. But there's no fun in an answer that simple, right? That's not to say that <i>can't</i> be the case. Just pointing out that a mystery should be a little more fun. Then again, that might be enough of a mystery to start, since regardless of who you are and how you got here, one fact is true for all of you.<br /> <br /> <b>You don't even know his name.</b><br /> <br /> Perhaps you just work at the funeral home and you're here to make sure everything goes smoothly. Maybe you received a text with a time and place from a contact you don't remember putting in your phone. It could be that you're not even here for the deceased, but someone\u2014or something\u2014 else. A cascade of unexpected circumstances could have landed you here, certainly. Weirder things have happened. And there's even a chance that you simply don't know why.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the circumstances of your arrival, there <i>is</i> one thing that I can say for certain: <b>This moment is going to change everything. </b>You might not know it ahead of time, but this is just the first of many dominoes to fall. Where the story goes I cannot say, because the future is a mystery. What exactly happens, how you shape it, and who you become are all up to you.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Your story starts and ends at a funeral. But it doesn't have to.\u200b</span></div> <br /> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce</span> <u>T</u>HE SETTIN<u>G</u></span></b></div> <br /> <div align=\"center\">\u2bcc \u2bce \u2bcc</div> <br /> <div align=\"center\">Los Angeles\u2014The City of Angels\u2014August 2025.\u200b</div> <br /> <br /> Los Angeles is the most populous county in America, surpassing the combined population of 40 other US states. The county's seat, Los Angeles, is the second most populous city in the United States behind New York, and is the heart of the film and TV industry. Though it's called The City of Angels, people who live here know that it's really The City of Dreams. Whether you're a transplant or LA-born and raised, if you live in the county, it's more than likely you at one point held a dream that was larger than life. Maybe you still do.<br /> <br /> But LA has its problems. Despite being one of the most diverse places in the US, it too falls short of the ideal of America as a melting pot. It's a city filled with as much ugliness as beauty, where the crime rate is high, economic inequality is rampant, and the echo chamber is vast.<br /> <br /> But this is a story about dreamers. Of people with a deep curiosity. A need to know. Some truth that they are searching for. Answers to a mystery.<br /> <br /> This is a story about <i>you</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce</span> <u>T</u>HEME<u>S</u></span></b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\"><b>\u200b \u2bcc IDENTITY</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> I knew from the start that identity was one of the main things I wanted to focus on for this Chronicle. I love character-driven stories, and the various Chronicles of Darkness game lines and the Storytelling System as a whole is geared toward exactly those kinds of stories. In particular, Mage centers the question of identity and how it is performed and mediated over time through the use of Shadow Names, the way Mage Sight is filtered by the Mage, and their Long-Term Nimbus. In Mage, everyone is given a Sympathetic Name, generally the name they were most often referred to as they first began to develop their own sense of consciousness and form connections to others as an individual. But that name is a product of the Lie, something ascribed to them to box them in. It's not until someone Awakens that they can, for the first time, decide who they are and who they want to be without being completely blinded by the world and its apparent limitations.<br /> <br /> Because of that, the choice of a Shadow Name and the ways it informs your Nimbus and Destiny are really special. Taking a Shadow Name is and should be a momentous step for any mage. It's not simply an alias or a nickname. You are informing the Supernal and reality exactly who you are and who you want to be and, consciously or not, inviting that into your life. But a Shadow Name and Nimbus aren't just something you choose once and never reflect on again. The way you act as a mage, the kind of spells you cast, and the Mysteries you choose to explore or ignore all come to refine and define your identity as a mage. There's a reason a person no longer has strong temporal sympathy to who they were before an Awakening, and the same should be true for a mage at the end of their career and at the start.<br /> <br /> For this Chronicle, I want to explore what it means for the characters to have this rare chance to define and redefine who they are on a symbolic and metaphysical level, as well as all of the trials and tribulations that come with that sort of ability.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\"><b>\u2bcc FREEDOM VS. CONTROL</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> This is the quintessential struggle in the Mage universe. There is no Ascension War, not unless you're an Archmaster navigating the Ententes and trying to seal your Omens to bring about the exact kind of world that you want to see. The grand struggle for the future of the Fallen World has long since been fought, way back in the Time Before. What we live in is the result, a world redefined in the aftermath of a cosmic war where all are slaves to the inexorable god-tyrants that rule from the Supernal. The overwhelming majority of people will never even know how much they've lost to the Abyss and the Lie the Exarchs have crafted. But mages have the rare blessing and curse of Awakening to the truth, of being able to peer past the Lie and see the bars of the cage. But for most mages, that Awakening is the first and last time they will ever touch the Supernal short of Archmastery.<br /> <br /> You've seen through the Lie, the glitch in the Matrix, and now you're back in the cage. What do you do? Like the man from the Allegory of the Cave, do you struggle against your chains, trying to enlighten your fellow prisoner and raise them up so that they, too, can one day touch the fundamental truths of the universe? Or do you throw in with your jailers instead, trading servitude for temporal power and the potential for eventual enlightenment at your masters' side?<br /> <br /> It's not just a long-term question, either. As a mage, you have the power to bend the rules of nature to your will. But you're not the only one. Mages form communities to mediate disputes, trade favors and knowledge, and keep each other in check. Everyone, regardless of their Order Status or lack of it, has some opinion on how mages should operate in the world. Should you be free to use magic as you wish in pursuit of your Obsessions?<br /> <br /> The thing about mages is that, unlike Sleepers, there's very little that they <i>can't</i> do if they apply themselves. No thought can be hidden, no hypothesis untested, no truth undiscovered. And that's why the question of freedom vs. control is such an important one. You and your kind can achieve just about anything you'd like.<br /> <br /> But <i>should </i>you?<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bcc THE ECHO CHAMBER</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> The phrase &quot;echo chamber&quot; is not one that's easy to avoid in the modern day. In the last few years, especially, it's become a common buzzword in both academic and popular discourse. And with good reason, because echo chambers are everywhere you look. We've all heard the term, know what it's referring to, and understand more or less what the problem is with falling victim to one. But how does one identify an echo chamber in the wild? If you're born into, raised in, or grow up in one, how do you escape? And when you do, what exactly does life look like on the outside?<br /> <br /> Mages call themselves The Wise, a term that is half aspirational and half ironic. Yet, despite being gifted with near unrivaled information gathering and truth seeking power, mage society is no less fractious than mundane society. At times it may even seem more so. For people with Platonic truths at their fingertips, why is it that mages can't ever seem to agree on anything?<br /> <br /> Magic is humanity's birthright. <i>No, humanity is magic</i>. Magic is a responsibility. <i>No, magic is payment.</i> Magic is a struggle. <i>No, magic is alive.</i><br /> <br /> For all the power they wield, mages are human\u30fcoften frighteningly so. The ability to manipulate the Fallen laws doesn't remove people's flaws. If anything, it only seems to heighten them because of the greater power mages have and the fewer restrictions on their actions. And what is more human than the desire to define oneself by what one is and is not, to draw lines and boundaries and categorize things in neat boxes in service of understanding? For all the discourse on echo chambers, academics fall victim to them just the same as the general public. Mages are no different.<br /> <br /> LA, in particular, is known for its political divisions. Instead of a unified Pentacle, it is governed by a Consilium and an Assembly locked in a bitter rivalry\u2013they fight over the ideal state of governance, Mysteries, and prospective members of all Orders in equal measure and ignore each other otherwise, only working together when absolutely necessary or to deal with mutual threats. The Seers, too, keep to themselves, more interested in their own plots and schemes than the spiritual descendants of their gods' ancient enemies. With lines drawn clearly in the sand and each Order its own isolated island, what are newly Awakened mages to do? How do they navigate the divided world they have Awakened in, the grand search for truth and meaning, and their own developing identity in a place where echo chambers and neotribalism are not only the reality but the expectation?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T12:50:11-07:00","id":1554741,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce</span> <u>T</u>HE CAS<u>T</u></span></b></div> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"372\" height=\"481\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/GCUw9R9.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/GCUw9R9.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/GCUw9R9.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\"><b>DERRIK THORPE (26) - HE/HIM - LAWYER</b></span></div> <div align=\"center\">(Played by Keni)\u200b<br /> <br /> </div> Derrik Thorpe has the look in his eye of someone who's seen a lot of things in his life and knows better than to talk about them. But don't let the dyed hair, piercings, and tattoos fool you; Derik is a softy, and likely more intimidated by strangers than they are by him. Originally from South Dakota, he and his mother moved to LA when he was a teenager and never looked back. Derrik graduated from UCLA with his JD but has yet to actually practice Law. The past two years have been\u2026 complicated, to say the least, with some very low lows and not much in the way of highs. But he's moved out of his mom's place, he's seeing a therapist, and his life seems to be getting back on track.<br /> <br /> Or it was until he received a letter in the mail containing two items. The first is an invitation to a funeral, the only information provided an address and a date written in embossed golden letters. The other is a polaroid of him and the other boys at a faith camp that he attended when he was fourteen back in South Dakota, an experience that he'd very much like to forget. And while that camp has long since shut down, the other boys' names forgotten, he can't help but feel that he knows exactly which one it is that died.<br /> <br /> Sure, Derrik hasn't really been around people in a long time, and he doesn't remember a polaroid being taken that day at camp, but the funeral seems like it might be fine. Who knows, he might even get the chance to ask the other boys some burning questions. What could go wrong?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <img width=\"372\" height=\"481\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/t025AKl.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/t025AKl.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/t025AKl.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\"><b>DAMIAN WHELAN (38) - HE/HIM - PRIVATE INVESTIGATOR</b></span>\u200b<br /> (Played by Xeno)\u200b<br /> </div> <br /> Damian's never met a bottle of hard liquor or a cigarette that he didn't like. He runs a private investigation business that he inherited from his dad, lives in a one-bedroom apartment in North Hollywood that reeks of cigarettes and booze, and his life partner is a guinea pig named Sam Spadey.<br /> <br /> Unlike our other protagonists, Damian's life is filled with work\u2013even with a business degree from UCLA, it's not easy running a 3 person business, especially when it's community-focused and you're paying your Gen Z employees living wages. What that means for Damian is a lot of long hours, late nights, and uncompensated overtime. It's an often thankless job, but maybe the satisfaction of making a difference for someone, even in a small way, makes up for it. If not, a smoke and a couple glasses of whiskey are usually enough to take the edge off after a particularly grueling day.<br /> <br /> Damian doesn't have the luxury of getting to do whatever he likes. Money's tight, which means when he gets an odd case, he's inclined to take it. And he's dealt with his fair share of\u2026 strange cases over the years. But this one's certainly new. Normally his clients call or ask to meet, but this one slipped an envelope under the door to the office, accompanied by an email from a throwaway account. $5000 to investigate the case of a guy who's died, some leads to follow up on, and a summary of the police report. The first half has already been deposited in his account. The second will be wired to him upon completion.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of secrecy on the part of his mystery client, and the funeral's rapidly approaching, but the money's already sitting comfortably in his account and the client just wants more information, not definitive answers. He'd be lying if he said he wasn't curious about what's going on. It should be an open and shut case. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <img width=\"372\" height=\"481\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/YYhJAxK.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/YYhJAxK.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/YYhJAxK.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\"><b>COLLIN WHITMAN (30) - HE/HIM - ANGEL INVESTOR</b></span>\u200b<br /> (Played by Screwy)\u200b</div> <br /> Collin has always been a little bit <i>eccentric</i>. He has certain habits and tendencies and needs things to be done a particular way or he freaks out. Luckily for him, Dave is there to take care of all the things he can't on his own. He and Dave met playing Dungeons and Dragons, and it wasn't long before Colin hired him to be his &quot;personal concierge.&quot; They naturally spend a lot of time together, and aside from the weekly D&amp;D sessions he plays, Dave is Collin's only contact with the outside world.<br /> <br /> Because of his peculiarities, Collin lives relatively off the grid. After his parents died, he got rich off the initial cryptocurrency boom and has not had to work since. Instead, he pursued an online degree in cryptography at UCLA and invested some of his shocking net worth into his tech bro D&amp;D buddies' startups, which all took off. Using their technologies, Dave's connections, and a sickening amount of money, Collin has established a life for himself of near total anonymity. He doesn't believe in lavish living or extravagance, preferring to eat and dress simply. His greatest expenditure is on security. He has a number of properties across the country, his presence has been scrubbed from the Internet, and nobody can find him unless he wants to be found.<br /> <br /> Or so he thought until a letter arrived for him 6 months ago. Though he was freaked out at first, Collin immediately recognized that it contained a cipher and decoded it, uncovering an address. When he mailed his response, a new ciphertext letter came from a different PO box in LA. This became a pattern, a game of coded messages and new addresses. Then his &quot;pen-pal&quot; went silent. A few days ago, Collin received a funeral invitation and realized what must have happened. It's been a while since he's been in public, but he's dying to know how his &quot;friend&quot; found him and what became of them.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T13:19:07-07:00","id":1554742,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce</span> 0 | <u>W</u>AKING WORLD DREA<u>M</u></b></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>\u2bcc</b> <b>0.0 | The Funeral</b></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">&quot;Your story begins and ends at a funeral. But it doesn't have to.&quot; - Anonymous</span><br /> <br /> <br /> \u2bcc \u2bce \u2bcc</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">There's nothing quite as terrifying and exciting as a first session, especially after a long period of not running games. Pros and amateurs alike struggle with getting things started. Players, too, feel a little bit of awkwardness and anxiety (in my experience) wondering how everything is going to fit together. Tons have been written about how to run an effective start to a campaign and whether opening around a table at a tavern is the greatest sin known to man or not. I like to do things differently, though. For me, the most exciting and interesting first sessions have always been the ones that started in unexpected places. And since the first session naturally sets the tone for the rest of the game, I figured it was important to set the stage right. So naturally, I figured the best way to kick off this wacky chronicle of mine would be to throw them into the deep end.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> Our first chapter starts <i>in medias res</i> as our three protagonists round a corner in the dark, lungs burning, hearts racing, running like their lives depend on it as men's screams ring out in the background\u2014one of them in pain, the other in growing horror. They're in some kind of dark passageway that smells of rust, dust, and mildew, with only the faint illumination of penlights they're carrying with them to guide the way. <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Damian</span>, at the front of the pack, notices a familiar stale, cloying scent accompanied by the sound of steady dripping. Approaching the nearest wall, he catches sight of a purplish-black, tar-like substance. Whatever it is, one look at it has him bolting at twice the speed.<br /> <br /> Behind him, <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Collin</span> catches sight of the dust and grime coating every surface and instinctively protects his face with his forearms, skin crawling. Which is fortuitous, because at that precise moment something barbed slices into the area where his face would have been, instead tearing through his sleeves and drawing blood. As he blinks through the pain, silvery motes seem to dance across the periphery of his vision.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Derrik</span>, at the back, looks over his shoulder to see a fourth and fifth figure running behind him. But the fifth doesn't quite round the bend as smoothly as the others did and is forced to brace himself to avoid slamming into it. As he looks ahead and meets Derrik, an unreadable expression on his face, something yanks him back into the shadows. The fourth figure, still a ways behind Derrik, shouts to the others to keep running and not turn back. Derrik is only too happy to oblige as he hears the familiar sound of electricity buzzing nearby.<br /> <br /> As Derrik overtakes Collin, he dances out of the way of a sparking cable that suddenly drops from the ceiling, shouting at the other man to run faster before he overtakes him, rapidly putting distance between them. Collin, noticing the sparking electrical box nearby, disregards the advice completely and stops to examine it for a switch or lever, figuring that getting some more illumination is his biggest priority at the moment. He fails to get the lights working (and when Screwy opts to take a Dramatic Failure) his hand connects with something causing a blinding flash of light to flood the area, bringing the scene to a close for him.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile at the front, Damian rapidly approaches a fork in the path as the corridor splits off in two directions. But just before the split is a 6 foot long pool of the substance he saw before. Rather than slow down, he takes a running leap and manages to just clear the edge on the other side. Both tunnels are crowned by dilapidated signs: one shows a downward arrow and the other a chain-like symbol. He decides to go with the former and the passageway, true to the sign, begins to slope downward, gently at first and then increasingly sharp. But the sound of rushing liquid behind him leaves no room for relief. Spotting what looks to be a service ladder leading to a hatch in the ceiling, he makes a leap and hangs off of it, trying his best to curl his body and make himself as small as possible as he presses himself against the hatch in the ceiling. A veritable torrent of the purplish-black substance rushes past where he was standing but moments ago. Seemingly in defiance of physics, the surface of this liquid rises higher and higher, threatening to reach him, but Damian is able to fumble with the lever and swing the latch open. He's blinded by light on the outside, just like Collin, crossing the threshold and leaving the scope of this scene.<br /> <br /> And then there was one. Derrik, unlike the others, is mainly focused on the ceiling, counting wires and deftly dodging side to side as sparking cables arc downward toward him one after another. In the distance, he sees the corridor end in a bend, a bright light shining from around the corner. Not seeing any other exits and fearing the rising crackle of electricity behind him, he dashes around the corner and joins the others in the light.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">And there we have the first scene of the chronicle! This scene had our first and only use of music for the first session, a tense and heart-pounding song that immediately ramped up the tension and put them in fight-or-flight mode. In retrospect I feel like I could have pushed it further, but for the first scene of the chronicle I think I did a pretty good job. The players certainly seemed to enjoy it.</span><br /> <br /> As the light clears, Collin finds himself disembodied in a void, the only sound he can hear a voice that echoes, <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">&quot;Guard the keys.&quot;</span> Soon, another joins in, then another, until they become a garbled cacophony. He shouts at them to stop and finds himself reliving a memory from several years back. His mom tells him that they'll talk when she gets back, looking apologetic. She leaves the handkerchief she painstakingly made for his father when they first started dating on the table in the entryway before leaving. The grandfather clock tolls five times and the dream begins to dissolve.<br /> <br /> It is night time now, and the monstrously large moon casts its silver glow on the clock, which grows larger and taller by the second until it becomes a towering lighthouse. As he tries to approach, looking for a door, Collin finds that oddly enough, he can't seem to make it any closer. But along its base he spots bushes of black roses and notes that all along its surface are silver barbs, as if the structure was designed to prevent anyone from scaling it. In the background, he can just barely make out the silhouettes of four other towering structures, but they're too far away to discern any details. All of a sudden, he hears the sound of shattering glass, an apology, and then sees his handkerchief, a red stain spreading across its surface. As he reaches down to pick it up, the dream ends.<br /> <br /> Collin jolts awake in the back seat of a rental car, clutching the pristine handkerchief in his hands as the driver, his personal assistant and confidant <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Dave</span>, peers at him in the mirror. Collin is understandably frazzled and tries, failing, to explain what he's seen. Asking Dave whether he's ever had any strange dreams, the man regales him with a story from college in which he had a stress dream about an elementary school teacher showing up in his common room and getting increasingly frantic when he couldn't find a first aid kit for her. Dave lets Collin know they've arrived at the location, and he looks out the window.<br /> <br /> Damian blinks awake on the couch, scotch glass still in hand and a noticeable stain on his dress shirt. Aside from a crick in his neck and burgeoning headache, he feels like his sleep was restful and dreamless. As he goes about his morning routine, though, he can't help but stumble around. Whether because of the hangover or something else, he keeps misjudging distances, stubbing toes on tables that should be further away and stopping a few feet short of where the door actually is. Despite these minor setbacks, he gets in the shower (Xeno notes that he is the type to brush and shower at the same time) and is ready to go with plenty of time to spare. On the way, he stops for two coffees and an egg sandwich and fields a call from <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Sarah</span>, his secretary.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Oh my god. </i>You'll never guess what.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...What?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No, that's not how this works. You have to guess.&quot;<br /> <br /> Damian correctly guesses that it's about <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Tomas</span>, her SpinCycle instructor, prompting her to note with awe that he <i>is</i> pretty good at his job. Apparently, Tomas had never had lasagna before, and she was angling to suggest bringing some for him next class when her eavesdropping archnemesis <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Linda</span> showed up. According to Linda, her mother's lasagna is legendary, and she used the secret family recipe as an excuse to get Tomas's number in<i> clear violation</i> of Sarah's dibs. Sarah, frustrated that her six month &quot;project&quot; is being threatened, references the other case the office is working on, suggesting that Damian's other worker <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Ollie</span> might have one more missing dog to look for if Linda doesn't back off. And it would be a favor to the dog, too, since she's seen her leave it in the car during class before. After confirming that Damian probably won't be in the office today, she seems to have gotten everything she needs and hangs up, leaving the private investigator to lament that he got absolutely nothing of value from the conversation.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Screwy thinks that she's a nuisance but I find her hilarious and Keni agrees.</span><br /> <br /> Derek, meanwhile, has woken up feeling surprisingly well-rested after a night of dreamless sleep in spite of having gone to bed especially late. He finds it odd that there is no alarm blaring, at which point he rolls over and discovers that both the clock and his phone seem to be dead. In fact, none of the clocks in his apartment are working.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Technology will always fail you when you need it most.</span><br /> <br /> Angrily shouting, as if to an imaginary friend who has done this to him, he runs outside to ask a neighbor for the time and learns that he has overslept his engagement. He runs back in and hastily throws on his suit, tossing his useless phone and running toward the door. This time, he notes, all the clocks in his apartment seem to be working and show the correct time, which causes him to scowl and unplug them all in retribution. As he's leaving the apartment, a familiar car tears away from the parking lot as if making a getaway, but he pretends to not see it as he's got far more important things to worry about. He picks the Aston Martin for today's engagement, plugging in the address of the funeral home, though he thinks it should be easy enough since it was a 3 minute walk the last time he checked. But instead he finds that his destination is somewhere completely different than he remembered, nearly an hour away. Texting his mom from his burner phone, he sprints to the nearest Metro station and catches the train instead. Inside he learns that the last stop, Union Station, is not in service due to some sort of problem. While waiting for the train, he looks it up and finds out that there's a notable police presence and some sort of investigation has been going on for the past week, though details are sparse.. Regardless, his train finally arrives and he hops on, hoping he won't be late.<br /> <br /> Collin takes in <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">The Bearers of the Sacred Heart</span> church, Neo-Gothic building of bluish-grey stone with rose windows, stained glass, and a steeple topped by a gold cross. It's dwarfed by the dull downtown buildings around it but protected by a stone wall and a wrought iron fence out front. It seems to be a nice little pocket of life in the midst of the bustling city. Collin, whose casual outfit is the fanciest thing he owns, is noticeably stressed out about the task before him. Still, he insists on doing it alone, but does ask Dave to watch over him until he enters. Before he does, though, he notes that one of the stained glass windows depicts a thorny bush crowned by five black roses. This naturally gets his gears turning. In the vestibule, he looks for an itinerary for the day or a pamphlet for the funeral and finds one, but oddly enough it does not have any sort of identifying information on it.<br /> <br /> Venturing further inside, he notes the latticed wooden beams on the ceiling, made to resemble the hull of a ship. It's a lovely church, and though he's a bit early, there's only one other person present. She appears to be a petite woman with dark brown skin, curly black hair, and hoop earrings. She's engrossed in a book that appears to be written in a foreign language\u2014Sanskrit, Collin thinks. She makes no move to converse or acknowledge his presence, so he initiates, proceeding to stumble through a conversation in which it seems like he can't decide whether he needs to explain his presence here or ask her to explain it to him. He admits that he doesn't actually know why he's here or who he's here for, even, which she notes is unusual.<br /> <br /> &quot;I believe the name you're looking for is <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Jacob Carver</span>.&quot; - Dr. Devi King, as she later introduces herself.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">This is the first of many meandering conversations with Collin during the session. His recollection of the dream to Dave was a little confusing, but the two of them know each other quite well and Dave has little issue parsing Collin's frenetic speech and seeming non-sequiturs. The other NPCs? Not so much.</span><br /> <br /> As Damian arrives some time later, he takes out a polaroid and stares at it for sometime before flipping it and examining the name on the back. He then puts it back in his jacket and gets ready to begin his investigation for real. By the time the church bells ring for the 10:00 am service, the pews are a little more filled than before. But the crowd is extremely thin, composed of somewhere between two and three dozen people in total. Two figures sit in the pews at the front, a woman in a rumpled business suit with a flawless face of makeup and a young woman in her 30s in a plain black dress au naturel. Everyone else seems to be interspersed between the front and the middle in awkward clusters with the exception of one gentleman in the far back sporting an expensive-looking blue suit and a gold watch. The priest, a man in his late 30s or early 40s with reddish brown hair and a trimmed beard, seems contemplative, staring out the stained glass windows up until the last chime of the bells. When it's time for the mass to start, he straightens up, assuming a more appropriate posture, and begins.<br /> <br /> It's some time later that Derrik finds himself sneaking into church, praying that nobody will pay attention to him. He slips into the pew at the very back at the opposite end of the man in the blue suit. They make eye contact and Derrik gives a small nod, becoming increasingly uncomfortable as the man maintains eye contact before smirking and averting his eyes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Come to me, all you who are weary and burdened, and I will give you rest. Take my yoke upon you and learn from me, for I am gentle and humble in heart, and you will find rest for your souls. For my yoke is easy and my burden is light.&quot; - Priest<br /> <br /> In an address to the audience, the priest reveals that of those gathered, he likely knew Jacob the least, and so there are very few words he can say to do justice to his memory. But he urges them to remember that this is a day for celebrating his life rather than just lamenting his passing, bringing up a story about another culture that cries in lament when a child is born and laughs with joy when they die. As he explains it, to be born into a world full of prejudice, suffering, and pain is a most terrible thing. But to be freed of that suffering at the end of one's life is, for those people, something to be celebrated. The priest says there is something we can all learn from them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">He's referring to the Trausi, one of the Thracian tribes described by Herodotus in <i>The Histories</i>. In the 1700s, William Cowper composed a poem entitled <i>The Thracian</i> about their culture, which I've reproduced below for those interested. Super fascinating stuff!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Thracian parents, at his birth,<br /> Mourn their babe with many a tear,<br /> But, with undissembled mirth,<br /> Place him breathless on his bier.<br /> <br /> Greece and Rome, with equal score,<br /> &quot;O the savages!&quot; exclaim,<br /> &quot;Whether they rejoice or mourn,<br /> Well entitled to the name!&quot;<br /> <br /> But the cause of this concern<br /> And this pleasure would they trace,<br /> Even they might somewhat learn<br /> From the savages of Thrace.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Damian pays little attention to the service, instead looking around at the crowd to see what he can glean. Aside from the family and the man at the back, who also seems to be scoping out the crowd and even briefly makes eye contact, there are only a few individuals that catch his eye. He sees Dr. King, who is still reading rather than paying attention to the service, as well as a group of three college age girls who seem to be whispering to each other and trying to be discreet. The girl in the center is a goth wearing a pentagram choker, the girl to her left is a doppelganger of her with shorter hair and fashion that's more goth-chic, and the one on the right seems to be dressed plainly and looking at the other two in exasperation.<br /> <br /> Collin, unlike Damian, is paying close attention to the service and does not like it one bit.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">In fact, Screwy went so far as to call the proceedings &quot;vanilla,&quot; harping on the priest's lack of familiarity with Jacob and his family and saying that it felt like the service was perfunctory at best. Keni found it to be a pretty normal service and thought the priest was just trying to do his best to connect with the crowd and offer his prayers in their time of need. I kept my thoughts on this one close to the vest, but I wouldn't exactly use the word &quot;perfunctory&quot; to describe a sermon in which allusions are made to 5th century historians' writings on the funerary traditions of different cultures.</span><br /> <br /> The most notable moment of the service is the part where the choir assembles. One lady in particular stands out among the others, tall and gaunt with black hair and dark eyes. She towers over the others in silence as they sing until it comes time for her solo. The entire audience, including the three whispering girls, are stunned into silence by the most melodic, soulful vocal performance any of them had ever heard. It begins in English but transitions to Latin partway through, and as it reaches a crescendo, the characters can <i>feel</i> the vibration of the notes resonating within their chests. As the song progresses and the audience listens in rapt silence, the singer hunches over, every movement of her body and note echoing from her lips brimming with raw emotion that somehow never gets in the way of the song. Tears stream down her face and she makes no attempt to wipe them. When the song ends, there is a resounding awestruck silence, broken only by the quiet sobbing of Mrs. Carver and Derrik's minute sniffing in the back pew. Collin makes eye contact with the singer, and with his background is able to make out some of the Latin lyrics. She seemed to be signing about the weight of souls and bearing burdens, but he doesn't know enough to grasp anything else.<br /> <br /> At about the two hour mark the service ends, but not before the priest repeats the verse from the beginning and reminds the audience that The Bearers of the Sacred Heart church takes community very seriously, and that its doors are open any day at any time for those in need. About half of the crowd immediately begins filing out, though the rest stick around, chatting in the clumps they had formed. Collin immediately rushes over to the soloist and showers her with praise, telling her with a conspiratorial wink that her performance was the one aspect of the funeral that actually had any soul.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Ouch. Sorry, pastor, that's what you get for holding an extremely <i>vanilla</i> service.</span><br /> <br /> Collin is under the impression that the singer, who reluctantly says he can call her Mary, must know the deceased given the depth of emotion in her performance. On the contrary, she tells him that she has no clue who he is but that funerals always get to her. After all, all these people have gathered to honor Jacob's memory but this might just be the last time a group of people this large ever think of him again. Isn't that just tragic?<br /> <br /> Collin, never one to back down from a situation, begins to explain how he was brought here by an invitation of mysterious provenance that likely has to do with a series of coded letters he received from an anonymous individual he assumes to be Jacob. Mary seems thoroughly confused by the explanation, which is twice as convoluted and rushed as it needs to be. But she humors him regardless and takes a look at the handwriting of the letters. After a good ten second pause, she tells him that she does not, in fact, recognize the handwriting.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't think I can actually be of help to you in figuring out whatever it is you're trying to. But I hope that you find it, whatever it is, and that it brings you peace.&quot; - Mary<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Awkward conversation number two. Thinking about how crazy Collin's story about the letters is to the average person never fails to make me laugh. Every time Keni and I talk about the game and bring Collin up, they can't help but mention how absolutely unhinged he sounds to a remotely normal person. Considering what a Mystery Play is like to those on the outside, even mages, it's very on brand. But notably, this is just the beginning. We haven't even gotten to the strange hallucinations freaky stuff yet. Also, note that Collin, despite his penchant for interrogating <i>everyone </i>he meets, never pauses to consider whether they're telling him the truth.</span><br /> <br /> While Collin is making people reflexively grip their purses a little bit tighter, Damian gets down to business. Based on the polaroid photo, which depicts a group of boys in their early-to-mid teens, any attendees of the funeral that were in it would probably be in their mid-to-late 20s now. There are only 3 people around who fit that age range, but none of them have the right hair color. Two of them are busy chatting with the goth squad, so he heads over to the boy in the back row of pews.<br /> <br /> &quot;Quite the service, huh?&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> &quot;Is that... a joke?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;I guess that depends. Is it funny?&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> There is a long beat as Derrik looks up at him. An awkward silence follows, which makes the man in the blue suit at the other end of the pew snicker.<br /> <br /> &quot;I apologize. Funerals make me uncomfortable.&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, it's okay. Y'know... Ch-churches make <i>me</i> uncomfortable.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">(Man in the Blue Suit: You didn't ask but awkward small talk makes <i>me</i> uncomfortable.)</span><br /> <br /> &quot;Did you know him?&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> &quot;I did, when I was like, a <i>kid</i>... What about\u2026 you, strange man?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;Unfortunately, I only knew him in passing.&quot;<br /> <br /> When Damian asks Derrik to tell him more about Jacob, the younger man looks uncomfortable and lowers his voice so as not to be heard. Noting this, Damian goes in for the kill.<br /> <br /> &quot;Listen, you don't have to be talking loudly in here, <i>Derrik</i>. Do you mind if we go outside?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Did\u2026 I give you my name?&quot; - Derrik, dread rising.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">At this point, I was ready to just sit back and eat some popcorn. I had talked back and forth with the players about their characters individually and had given a lot of thought to what possible dynamics might be, but I wasn't exactly sure how they would all slot together. For all the elements the player characters share, they also have a ton of differences and possible points of contention. I also had no specific plan for how they would all gather and form a group, preferring to let the interactions play out and only step in if a guiding hand was necessary. Having Damian approach Derrik like this and throw out his name to unnerve him made him click for me and in that moment I could instantly see how this dynamic was going to work in the long term.</span><br /> <br /> &quot;I figured it out.&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah. (clearing throat) Funny thing about that.<i> I'm not going anywhere with you</i>.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;Not even to the outside of a church?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No, sir. Whatever the f-<i>frack</i> your name is.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You can call me Damian.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wow, they allowed you in church?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;I know, shocker.&quot; - Damian, earning another laugh from the man at the other end of the pew.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">This is a reference that's going to come up again and again in this chronicle, I just know it.</span><br /> <br /> &quot;Sooo... are you going to tell me how you know my name?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> Damian takes out the photo of the boys out from his coat and hands it over, explaining that his current client is looking for information about Jacob, which Derrik insists <i>so convincingly</i> that he won't be able to provide. Damian is skeptical, figuring that there must be something he can share that'll give him a potential clue. But Derrik says that he doesn't really remember Jacob. They were kids at a church camp ages ago.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can clearly see it in the picture. It says 'Whispering Pines Faith Camp' on those gaudy T-shirts.&quot;<br /> <br /> Except the polaroid he's looking at is not the one he remembers. It depicts five boys in the summertime playing by a creek. Two of them stand out front, one looking a bit blurry around the edges. They seem unaware of the camera, sporting large white T-shirts that are too big for their lanky bodies. But there isn't any writing on the shirts at all. Derrik flips the photo as if he's expecting the correct image to be on the other side, but all he sees is a sticky note with the words &quot;Person of Interest: Derrik Thorpe&quot; on it.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't understand. Someone gave you an edited photo?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;Is there anything else that's off about it?&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you part of some organization I need to know about, and do I need a lawyer?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">What an oddly specific set of questions to ask in this situation. What kind of organizations have you been dealing with, Derrik?</span><br /> <br /> At this point Damian hands him a business card for Whelan Investigations, hoping to reassure him that he's not actually in any sort of trouble: &quot;I can assure you you don't need a lawyer. I'm just looking for information.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Then start asking the right questions, I guess. I'm not leaving this church with you, though.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> Damian asks if he can have a seat and Derrik, while still uncomfortable, acquiesces. As he scoots aside, he gives the man in the tailored suit a look, trying to see if he'll finally leave them alone or if he's just decided to enjoy the show. The man returns his look and seems to misunderstand Derrik's intentions, scooting all the way across the pew to sit beside him. Now Derrik is sandwiched between <i>two </i>men he doesn't know with no easy means of escape.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"372\" height=\"481\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/0OaHM8a.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/0OaHM8a.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/0OaHM8a.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;It looks like the two of you were having a fun conversation and I... figured I might, you know, butt in a little bit. Felt rude to eavesdrop.&quot; - Man in the Tailored Suit<br /> <br /> Derrik seems to curl into himself, face getting red as he processes the situation and tries to figure out what to do. He goes to introduce himself, offering a hand, but stops as the man reaches into his pocket and proffers his fist, three chocolate Tootsie Pops sticking out from between his fingers like he's Wolverine. Derrik says his mom taught him not to take candy from strangers, but Damian has no such qualms. The suited man gives him one and unwraps the remaining two, popping them in his mouth. Derrik makes a face at that..<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Later, Keni told me that Derrik, seeing him eat his own Tootsie Pops, figured they weren't actually poisoned or drugged and then felt extreme FOMO. But he was too embarrassed and prideful to ask for one in the end. Poor guy. Maybe if he runs into the suited man again he'll have another chance.</span><br /> <br /> &quot;What can you tell me about this 'Whispering Pine'?&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> Derrik doesn't seem particularly enthused about responding but gives a perfunctory answer nonetheless. It was a faith camp in South Dakota with a bunch of activities, including hiking, archery, horseback riding, and canoeing.<br /> <br /> &quot;Bible reading?&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> &quot;And singing.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;Sounds awful.&quot; - The Suited Man<br /> <br /> &quot;The forest was nice, at least. I liked hiking. Archery was fun\u2014Sorry, this has nothing\u2014I don't know why you want to know about the camp.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, I don't either, honestly, but I'm <i>fascinated</i>.&quot; - The Suited Man<br /> <br /> Derrik is surprised that Jacob had moved to LA as well, and it comes out that he was a student at UCLA. Derrik, who <i>also</i> went to UCLA, seems incredibly uncomfortable about that but says coincidences happen all the time. He asks again whether he should have a lawyer present, to which the suited man mentions that he knows a couple that might be able to help if he needs it. Derrik is not pleased about the &quot;creepy old man&quot; (Damian) asking him questions, and being in the same age bracket, the other man, who introduces himself as <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Sam</span>, takes mock offense to the statement.<br /> <br /> Derrik surreptitiously sends a mayday text to his mom asking if he should answer questions about &quot;the guy&quot; or if he needs her there. Unfortunately, her phone is set to Do Not Disturb, which means she's probably working on a case. He gets a helpful automated response a few seconds later saying that she'll be back soon. Figuring it's better to be safe than sorry, he opens his Voice Memo app and begins recording the conversation. Meanwhile, Sam waves to Collin, beckoning him to approach the pews in the back.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hi... Did you need something?&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> &quot;Not particularly, but you looked kinda lost, so I figured you might know each other.&quot; - Sam<br /> <br /> Collin introduces himself and explains that he knew Jacob through a &quot;cryptographic game&quot; they played where they sent coded letters to each other. The &quot;letters&quot; were actually ciphertext containing an encoded address. For the past 6 months, Collin had been exchanging letters with Jacob by cracking the codes in them and mailing his responses to the addresses contained within. Once he did, he'd get another letter back containing a new encoded address. Notably, there wasn't any actual conversation going on in these exchanges, as Jacob never introduced himself and most of the letters seemed like little more than random anecdotes. The most recent of Jacob's letters simply described a pet that had grown too big for its enclosure and broken through the gate, but that had ultimately been found in spite of the frustration on the part of his mother.<br /> <br /> The only deviation from that pattern was the most recent letter Collin received, one written in a different hand and only containing a date and location. Damian at this point waves Collin off, explaining that it was written by Sarah, his secretary. He says that he was hoping that by talking to the two of them, he could get to the bottom of what actually happened to Jacob Carver.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Collin's lack of a reaction to this stranger's secretary sending him a letter inviting him to the funeral is fascinating. As we've established, he's a pretty odd guy and you never know exactly what he'll latch onto and what he doesn't really care about. As long as it doesn't work against him or his interests, he's usually unconcerned when strange things happen. Notably, I feel like this entire Story would have gone very differently had he followed up on this thread right then and there.</span><br /> <br /> &quot;So let me get this straight. The <i>actual</i> messages weren't important but you were finding hidden addresses in messages that you would then send letters to... and then <i>more</i> letters would come that just had addresses in them that you would... continue sending letters to?&quot; - Sam<br /> <br /> &quot;Mhm!&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> &quot;And you did this because?&quot; - Sam<br /> <br /> &quot;It was a challenge.&quot; - Collin, shrugging<br /> <br /> &quot;How did he even find you?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> Collin shrugs once again, and the two of them get into a small argument, with Derrik saying Collin has no sense of personal security and risk if he's getting mail from people like that and responding to it. Collin says that his security is actually state of the art, thank you very much.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Derrik has a point here, but so does Collin. He has a bunch of dots designed to give him anonymity despite his impressive net worth. The fact that someone was able to find him and knew enough about him to send encoded messages for him to crack is surprising. I'd be pretty curious about the sender too in his position.</span><br /> <br /> &quot;I feel like you don't really have a leg to stand on, though, because aren't you in a picture that this guy brought to you just now?&quot; - Sam<br /> <br /> &quot;I never said I was in the photo.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> Damian examines the polaroid closely. Though he's got a different hair color, the less blurry of the two kids in front definitely could be Derrik ten or so odd years ago. He turns the photo to Sam for inspection, and he seems pretty certain about the resemblance. After noting that he doesn't get the connection between kids at a summer camp in South Dakota and Jacob, Derrik rather helpfully shares that the slightly blurry kid next to him in the photo is none other than the dearly departed himself.<br /> <br /> &quot;He was very good at cryptography!&quot; - Collin, unprompted<br /> <br /> &quot;Did... you have a cryptography seminar at this faith camp? A little FBI feeder program or something?&quot; - Sam<br /> <br /> &quot;Those are just myths.&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> Derrik pulls out his own fancy invitation to the funeral and the polaroid <i>he</i> received. It looks almost identical to Damian's aside from the text reading &quot;Whispering Pines Faith Camp&quot; and the cross on the boys' T-shirts.<br /> <br /> As they talk, iIt comes out that Collin also went to UCLA, though virtually in his case.<br /> <br /> &quot;Man, everyone here seems to be going to UCLA.&quot; - Sam<br /> <br /> &quot;They have a great cryptography program. Normally it's in-person, but I was able to petition, because of the pandemic, to do it online.&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> They get into another little argument, with Derrik saying that Collin is lacking in self-preservation and Collin saying that he hasn't shared anything that couldn't be found online if someone wanted to find it out. Derrik says he's just trying to look out for him and calls him weird. The awkward silence is broken by him laying down his polaroid next to the other for people to compare.<br /> <br /> Collin notices that there are some minor physical differences between the polaroids and some artifacting taking place within the images, but the thing that stands out to him is that the location of the boys in the pictures is ever so slightly different between the two. He feels confident that these aren't actually the same photo taken in the same place at the same time. He also feels certain that Jacob, the blurry boy, has been inserted into the photo digitally afterward. That is likely why he appears to be a bit blurry and why there's a difference in contrast between him and the other boys.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Screwy chose to take a Dramatic Failure on his Investigation roll and I was excited to give him this description. Unlike most people, I like to give a lot of information on a botched roll. And though I don't always explain as much, that information is not necessarily useless either. Sometimes a Dramatically Failed roll can even get you a more expedient clue than if you'd succeeded, if you know how to work with it and are willing to puzzle out the truth.</span><br /> <br /> Damian gets a markedly different read on the polaroids. He notes that the actual polaroid film seems to be different between the two pictures. Derrik's, the one with the logo and camp name, appears to have been taken on a newer polaroid or at least using new film. The one Damian received seems more like vintage polaroid film. As he looks closer, he also notices that the locations appear to be similar but that it isn't a 1:1 correspondence.<br /> <br /> The locations are definitely analogous, and if you're not paying close attention to the background you'd miss it, but the trees in his polaroid are slightly different from those in Derrik's... as if they were in the same family of trees but not the exact same ones. It almost seems like someone took two separate sets of photos in similar locations and arranged it so that the kids were in the exact same poses and wearing the same kind of shirts, only one set didn't have the logos on them. But why would they do that? And how?<br /> <br /> &quot;They're polaroids. You can't edit a polaroid...&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm pretty sure you can, actually. I've seen digital polaroids at the store before where you can take a picture and decide if you like it or not, add touch ups, and then it prints it out afterward.&quot; - Sam<br /> <br /> Collin helpfully points out that they certainly didn't have digital polaroids around 15 years ago when these photos would have been taken, though the conversation is derailed a bit as Derrik calls the technology old and suggests only old people were using them in the 2010s in the first place. Sam is wounded, but Collin says he'll live.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait, you said someone sent this to you. How do you know this is actually you?&quot; - Sam<br /> <br /> &quot;Because I remember the day.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, if you remember this day, then you remember who took the photo, right?&quot; - Sam<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't remember any adults being around when we were out hiking... I don't remember any pictures being taken of me. I was a kid, I don't know.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;Then... isn't it possible it's not actually a picture of you?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I recognize these kids. I recognize *me*.&quot;- Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;But you said you didn't remember Jacob, right?&quot; - Sam<br /> <br /> &quot;I didn't remember his name, okay? I didn't really stay in contact with anyone after that.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> When the others ask, he says he stopped believing in &quot;this junk,&quot; his eyes roving around the church. They mostly shrug, not prying any further, and Derrik visibly relaxes, as if he were expecting more resistance. Damian senses that he's given them the Spark Notes version of the story and that he's visibly uncomfortable talking about it, leading him to reason that something traumatic must have happened while he was at camp all those years ago.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh. I have something to talk to Father Bennett about, so I'm gonna go talk to him for a little bit, but I'll be back if you guys are still chatting\u2026&quot; - Sam<br /> <br /> &quot;Derrik, do these letters spark any memories for you? Maybe he interlaced memories that you might recognize.&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> &quot;What, like a drug!? Is this coated? IS THIS COATED?&quot; - Derrik, panicking.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Inter</i>laced. Meaning, &quot;weaved into the letters,&quot; like stories or memories. Not <i>laced</i> with anything.&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, sorry. Look, I don't know what you do with your free time, dude.&quot; - Derrik.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yoga, actually. And a lot of D&amp;D.&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> &quot;I didn't know you were a demon-worshipping nerd.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> What follows is Derrik being possessed by the spirit of a Christian fundamentalist from the 80s and spewing classic talking points, at which point Collin stands up for himself and says that it's called the Satanic Panic, is rooted in nothing but prejudice, and is an attempt to control people via policing their interests and hobbies.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't know. My mom told me to stay away from stuff like that, so. That's cool, dude, but just don't bring it around me.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">This was a hilarious tangent that I could have never seen coming. Suddenly Derrik's faith camp experiences seem a lot more sinister given his gut reaction to D&amp;D in 2025. But the Satanic Panic isn't at all out of place in a story about echo chambers. You might even be surprised at the synchronicities between some of the most famous cases that lead to the panic and the series of events that our player characters are dealing with right now.</span><br /> <br /> A girl comes up to them from behind, making her presence known to the group. She's Black and in her mid-to-late 20s, with well-defined arms and long braids interspersed with purple streaks and golden accessories. Derrik hurriedly puts away his photo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"372\" height=\"481\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9KpsRzz.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9KpsRzz.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9KpsRzz.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I've never seen you guys around. Are you students, too? Friends of family?&quot; - Girl<br /> <br /> &quot;Student, yes. Trying to figure out connections.&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> She goes to give him a pat on the shoulder and he shudders, rubbing his arm and stammering incoherently for a good 10 seconds. Derrik jokes that he's got shingles, and after Collin explains that he's not a touchy person, she apologizes and introduces herself as <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Abigail</span>. She's a current History student at UCLA interested in Ancient Rome and Greece in particular.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Xeno: Wow, just like every other History student. What's your favorite mythology?</span><br /> <br /> &quot;I'm thinking of writing my dissertation on bonds of fraternity in soldier formations.&quot; - Abigail<br /> <br /> Returning to the original topic of conversation, she explains that she was in a different department than Jacob but that they were clubmates in &quot;The Phalanx.&quot; Though Collin guesses cryptography for Jacob, Abigail is surprised that there's even a program for that at UCLA. She says that he was a first year Anthropology grad student. The Phalanx, she explains, is a vaguely Greco-Roman themed social club that you can apply to that has housing off campus. She met Jacob through a mutual friend who was in class with him, he applied, and the rest was history.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm sorry for your loss.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;It honestly doesn't feel real yet, if that makes sense...&quot; - Abigail<br /> <br /> Collin, based on something Damian said earlier, mentions how odd it is for a person his age to die of a heart attack. According to him, usually in the case of a young person there's some kind of misfiring of nerves or deeper underlying issues. A dark look crosses Abigail's face as she listens to his explanation, and Derrik tells him to lay off.<br /> <br /> Abigail says it's fine, but that he drank a lot that night because it was his birthday and he'd decided to throw a rager. Apparently Jacob wasn't really the type to party or drink, and he might have overdone it. Damian asks if she saw him at the party and she confirms that everyone did. There aren't very many members of The Phalanx and they're a pretty tight-knit bunch, so there were plenty of witnesses to his inebriation.<br /> <br /> &quot;Did you take any photos?&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> &quot;At... the party? No, I don't think we did. We tend to follow Fight Club rules at the Legion House.&quot; - Abigail<br /> <br /> She does note that he vanished about halfway through the party, and that he wasn't in any condition to drive. Derrik wants to know who found him, which seems to make her very uncomfortable. She scans the area around them nervously but decides to share that the police apparently came by after the fact and said that he'd been found at Union Station. Try as she might, she can't figure out why he'd head all the way across town at that time of night. But it was one of the workers who found him in the morning in an old service tunnel.<br /> <br /> &quot;If I'm being honest, this probably has something to do with his project.&quot; - Abigail<br /> <br /> &quot;Anthropology?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;My friend, who's in class with him, says they're doing a year-long project for class, collecting urban legends and stuff. You know how every major city has stories about abandoned train tunnels under the city that might be ruled by lizard people or\u2026 whoever controls the airwaves or whatever? You know, conspiracy theory stuff?&quot; - Abigail<br /> <br /> As they chat, the group realizes that everyone present is a current or previous student of UCLA, though Derrik says he doesn't believe Collin's degree is real, so it might not count. As they bicker about cryptography, it comes out that Collin was &quot;pen-pals&quot; of a sort with Jacob, but Abigail doesn't remember him talking about anything like that. He was one of those people who was part of the group but kept to the periphery, she explains. They had a room for him at the Legion House, but he never used it, preferring to keep to himself.<br /> <br /> &quot;You said he was never one for parties before? Did you notice anything else?&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> He watches as her eyes dart around, as if something has come to mind that she'd rather not divulge. But he decides against pressing the issue, and Derrik steers the conversation away from it entirely by asking to exchange numbers, which she's glad to do.<br /> <br /> &quot;He was going through some personal stuff. Unrelated, I think, but maybe that's also why he went so hard on his birthday? Like I said, he liked his own personal space, didn't like when people pried. But I think there might have been some\u2026 relationship issues involved, too.&quot; - Abigail<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Abigail doesn't seem to know who the other person is. But she says her friend <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Deeanne</span> is likely to know, since she's the kind of girl who's always on top of the latest drama. Derrik can't help but be reminded of someone that he used to know.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm definitely not the kind of person who has time for stuff like that. I need to keep my scholarship.&quot; - Abigail<br /> <br /> At about this time, Collin is certain that he remembers Derrik's face from his dream. And he decides to broach the subject in the way that only an eccentric guy like Collin can.<br /> <br /> &quot;...Very weird, not for me, but probably for you, Derrik. I mean, something tells me you don't have a very open imagination. Something tells me you're very... in the box. Do you have weird nightmares recently?&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> &quot;Nope. Never had a... Nope. No.&quot; - Derrik, unconvincingly<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait... dreams? I think one of the topics he was thinking about choosing was dreams and sleepwalking, lucid dreaming, that kind of thing.&quot; - Abigail<br /> <br /> As Collin and Derrik get into another squabble and Damian gets dragged in as well, Abigail decides that she's put up with enough of the awkwardness and flees with a quick, &quot;Excelsior!&quot; Collin tries desperately to call to mind the finer details of his dream from the previous night, but the only most significant thing he can remember is &quot;keys.&quot; Nonetheless, he begins to regale Damian and Derrik with a long and confusing explanation of his history of weird lucid dreams that have only been increasing in frequency lately and which he's implying are connected to this case. Naturally, he sounds <i>insane</i>. Just as he finishes, the bell in the steeple above rings five times in quick succession.<br /> <br /> At the altar, the priest and Sam stop their heated conversation, turning in unison to stare intensely at Collin. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">When we first finished the session, I couldn't help but think of all the things I could have done differently, but looking back on it I enjoyed the first chapter very much. It was also a perfect reminder of the fact that even the most perfectly laid plan *never* survives contact with the player characters. I tend to be a Storyteller who both prepares mountains of content that may never see the light of day and does a lot of improv in the moment during a session (often causing all of that preparation to be useless), so I knew better than to script out how things would go. Rather than a plot, I just had a scenario with a mysterious death (and the explanation for what's actually going on), and various places and people of potential interest for the characters to explore or not depending on their goals.<br /> <br /> I was perfectly fine with them all abandoning the mystery and focusing on something completely different if they wanted to (though I knew there was no way they would do that). What I didn't expect was for them to stay in the church for so long or reveal their connections to Jacob so soon. I figured they'd keep their cards closer to the vest and chat up the NPCs a little more before gathering, but Damian was a man with a mission and jumped right to business with his prime suspects. Can't fault him for the efficiency, and it certainly led to some interesting information being revealed.<br /> <br /> In any case, that was the first chapter! Sorry for the length; I have a chronic issue with being concise. But since this is the first session, a nice long chapter is forgivable, right? I'll try to post these weekly, though if people enjoy the content and want to know more, I'm more than happy to share fun bits of lore and info about the setting, mysteries, and Storyteller Characters past, present, and future in-between posts.<br /> <br /> There's a bunch of foreshadowing and a ton of clues and hints in here that an experienced Mage player or ST might be able to put together that my players would never be able to figure out at this stage. I'm curious what people think is happening in my version of Los Angeles through a looking glass, darkly.<br /> <br /> Oh, and for those who would rather read the entire thing from start to end in one place uninterrupted, I'll keep this link updated with all the writeups I post:</span><span style=\"color:#16a085\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IqgctpGGtXv1KvqLciYm8OeyogN1PLWAplpa_80_KaQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":28942,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","user":"synchrosanct","date":". 10-28-2025, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T17:04:40-07:00","id":1554748,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>\u2bcc</b> <b>0.1 | Back to School</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u201cThe most beautiful thing we can experience is the mysterious. It is the source of all true art and all science. He to whom this emotion is a stranger, who can no longer pause to wonder and stand rapt in awe, is as good as dead: his eyes are closed.\u201d \u2015 Albert Einstein</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <br /> \u2bcc \u2bce \u2bcc</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Five bells ring in quick succession, bouncing off the walls of the church discordantly, as if transposed into a minor key. Collin catches sight of the priest and Sam at the front, pausing their tense conversation just in time to make eye contact with him as the bells cease their ringing. They turn to face away from him and resume their heated conversation, leaving Collin feeling incredibly concerned. He can't help but feel like the bells sound just like the grandfather clock from his dream.<br /> <br /> Derrik, noticing the sweat beading on his forehead, asks if everything's okay.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't necessarily believe in coincidence. I also don't believe in the supernatural per se, but...&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Collin, as usual, is king of the casual non-sequitur.</span><br /> <br /> Derrik, predictably, bristles at the weird man reacting to things nobody else can see.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's not my fault that you can't see it yet.&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Yet, he says, as if he knows that the others will join him on Delulu Island soon enough. In all fairness, though, Collin did dream about them, even if his memories are a little hazy. And if you dreamed it, it must be real, right???</span><br /> <br /> &quot;Ohhhh, you're craaaaazy. Ohhhh, got it. I recommend a therapist.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">I have to give it to Keni; the delivery of that line was insane. Almost as insane as Collin.</span><br /> <br /> &quot;Who doesn't?&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> &quot;I think Damian doesn't?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> As if in response, Damian goes to light up a cigarette, prompting discussion about proper etiquette in church. Damian questions whether one is allowed to do anything in the House of God.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Probably not, Damian. Probably not.</span><br /> <br /> Collin has honed in on Union Station as a major point of interest and thinks that his letters are some sort of key. So he turns to Damian and voices the idea that\u2019s been brewing in his head.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think I should go with you because I think there might be something down there that might need decoding.&quot;<br /> <br /> As he and Damian make plans, Derrik gets increasingly bad vibes from the two of them and decides now is as good a time as any to bolt. Unfortunately, he fails the roll to sneak away and Keni chooses to take a Dramatic Failure. As he tries to climb back over the pew without alerting them, he loses his balance and nearly cracks his head open on the tiled floor like Humpty Dumpty. 13 pairs of eyes (plus Damian and Collin) look back at the final row of pews as the noise reverberates throughout the space.<br /> <br /> After righting himself, pushing down the embarrassment, and going off on Collin about his crazy theories, Derrik stalks off to talk to the family of the deceased.<br /> <br /> &quot;Non-intellectuals, am I right?&quot; - Collin, to Damian, whose silence is pointed.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Ouch!</span><br /> <br /> Up at the front, the priest and Sam seem to still be engrossed in their conversation, though with their hushed voices it's hard to make out what they're saying. Jacob's mother and sister sit in silence at the front, the former with a full face of makeup and the latter going all natural and busy scrolling on social media. Derrik strikes up a conversation with Mrs. Carver, and he's almost a completely different person than the guy who was just talking to Damian, Collin, and Sam. He tells her that she probably doesn't know who he is but that he went to summer camp with her son when they were kids.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're Derrik! Oh, Jacob... he had so much to say about you. It's lovely to see you, honey.&quot; - Mrs. Carver<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">I can still see Keni's face in my mind, eyes boggling as Derrik reacts to the fact that he was a known quantity. Mrs. Carver scoops him up into a massive hug, not letting him go until she is forcibly removed.</span><br /> <br /> When Derrik says that he hasn't seen Jacob in years, she seems... confused.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, really? I recall him saying he went to visit you... My brain is all over the place, you'll have to forgive me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The tension creeps back into Derrik's voice and shoulders. He certainly wasn't privy to any visits recently... or ever. He goes on the defensive as he tries to process all of this new information, the conversation having quickly spiralled in a direction he couldn\u2019t have possibly guessed. Eventually there\u2019s a lull in the conversation and just as Derrik\u2019s let down his guard, Mrs. Carver delivers her third sucker punch of the conversation.<br /> <br /> &quot;How's Elaine doing?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">That would be Derrik\u2019s mother.</span><br /> <br /> Derrik, once again, looks like he wants to melt into the floor and/or die on the spot at the mention of his mother. How does she know his mother? They moved across states soon after that summer camp ended and there was no communication between the two families, at least as far as he\u2019s aware. His cortisol is spiking through the roof at this point.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">So a pretty normal day for Derrik.</span><br /> <br /> Derrik fields some questions about himself as he wrestles the rising panic within him, letting Mrs. Carver knows that he's recently moved into his own apartment, which she seems very excited about. We get the first mention of Derrik's father in the Chronicle here, too. Mrs. Carver implies that things must have been tough for Elaine with the situation with Derrik\u2019s father, to which Derrik says that his dad hasn't been around since he was a child. He hardly even remembers what he looks like.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Fathers and sons, Collin is on the lookout for iconography that \u201cdoesn't fit\u201d... He's got this idea in his head that something about the church is wrong. In his words, everything feels generic, like you could go to any online store and just buy everything in here. At this point the others begin pointing out how they think his OOC relationship with Christianity is coloring his character's perceptions of the church and the funeral service. Keni, in particular, points out the latticed rafters made to look like a ship. How on earth is that generic?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">This is somewhat of a running joke in the games we play together. Screwy has a tendency of playing religious characters in a very.... fascinating way. Which is to say that he somehow manages to invent and reinvent Christianity every time, or at least his version of Christianity. This happens whether or not there is a Christianity analogue in the setting and is most certainly not on purpose. So it is hilarious that the first time he plays in a setting where Christianity actually exists, he finds it utterly boring and generic. I will say, despite the hilarity of the situation and many of Keni and Xeno's criticisms being accurate, Screwy isn't exactly wrong. I tried to make the priest and the sermon a little reserved and understated, though at this point it's almost a meme how &quot;soulless&quot; the church is. So when he failed his Perception check and opted for a Dramatic Failure, I took it as the perfect opportunity to play with his thoughts about the church.</span><br /> <br /> As he stares at the statue of Jesus at the back, he quickly realizes that the crown of thorns on his head are made of silver. And as his eyes catch on the glinting metal...<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Drip\u2026</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2026Drip..</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:80px\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">.......Drip.</span></div> <br /> Beads of crimson begin to bloom and fall to the ground, forming a small pool of blood.<br /> <br /> Collin freaks out about the blood of Christ, as any sane man would, reaching for Damian to try and point it out to him. Damian reflexively slaps him on the shoulder and then asks if he's alright.<br /> <br /> &quot;Look at the Jesus statue.&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, he's been dead for a long time.&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">This is one of my favorite lines.</span><br /> <br /> &quot;Collins, that's your name, right? Are you well?&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">No, he's not well. That man has not been well in quite some time. That's also not his name, but Collin will not correct him for quite some time.</span><br /> <br /> As a growing sense of dread curls in the base of his stomach, Collin sees the puddle of blood shrink as individual droplets flow up through the air in defiance of gravity, flowing back into the crown before it fades back to its normal color. That only freaks Collin out even more, though of course nobody else can see it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">How's <i>that</i> for generic church service?</span><br /> <br /> Getting back on track, Collin determines that the best time to search Union Station would be very late at night or just as the building is opening in the morning. He offhandedly says that Damian looks like he's probably better at getting into places unnoticed.<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you saying I look shady?&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> &quot;I mean, the scruff isn't helping. But I'm sure you're very good at your job.&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> Damian recalls that Jacob was found in a service tunnel by a worker, someplace the average person wouldn't even know existed. As he talks to Collin, he notices the not fully goth girl trio he saw earlier during the service heading out, the leader seemingly worked up about something as they enter the vestibule. He decides to sneak up and eavesdrop on them all private investigator-like.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh my god, I got a really dark vibe from the front just now.&quot; - Goth leader<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, yeah, totally, I... I totally sensed a dark vibe from the front... too?&quot; - Doppelganger<br /> <br /> The third one looks at the other two with a puzzled expression.<br /> <br /> &quot;No, seriously, something about this place is off and I can't exactly place what it is.&quot; - Leader<br /> <br /> Suddenly, she seems to sense that someone's observing them. But as she calls out, Damian decides it's time to sneak back to the pews and pretend he's a totally normal human being who is not up to anything suspicious. The goth leader peeks her head out from the vestibule area and stares at him, but he does not turn around.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">It's unfortunate that nobody got to talk to this trio during the funeral. Having Abigail as the only source of info on Jacob aside from his mother will certainly skew the direction of the investigation in this and future chapters, though the characters do not realize it yet. But it makes perfect sense in character: Derrik got accosted by Damian before he could interact with anyone else and is now occupied talking to the family. Collin is not the best at talking to people and has decided that the train station is where all the answers will be. And Damian is operating off information from his client that indicates Derrik and Collin are the two persons of interest, so a group of mostly goth girls isn't his biggest priority. Plus, I imagine the leader's tonality and manner of speech remind him of Sarah, his Gen Z secretary, who he has opinions about. If the characters hadn't already spent the equivalent of a whole session in the church already, maybe I'd have had them chat up the boys. But we've got other people to talk to, places to go, and things to see, so I decided to move things along.</span><br /> <br /> Back at the front, Derrik mentions that he just passed the bar and Mrs. Carver is thrilled.<br /> <br /> Still unable to figure out what's up with Sam and the priest, Derrik decides to see if he can get some more information from Mrs. Carver. Unfortunately, all she can say is that he looks familiar, though she can't quite place where she recognizes him from. She begins to fan herself absently.<br /> <br /> &quot;Is it hot in here or is it just me?&quot; - Mrs. Carver<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">I don't know if it was the connotations that sentence has or my expression or tonality, but from this moment on everyone started thinking Mrs. Carver was a cougar trying to land Derrik at her son's funeral. Which was not my intention at all, but hilarious, and I decided to roll with the punches.</span><br /> <br /> As it so happens, it is quite cool in the church. The space is heavily air conditioned. Derrik, assuming hot flashes, suggests soy milk, which his mom swears by. Speaking of Elaine, Mrs. Carver asks Derrik if he can put them in touch since with Jacob's passing there's lots of legal stuff to take care of. Derrik gives her his mother's number (notably, one of her work numbers), and receives a little electric shock when he makes contact with her phone. He then proceeds to make a huge deal of it, reaching for an explanation for why he experienced an electric shock that nobody would have noticed or even thought about had he not drawn attention to it in the first place.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Nicely done.</span><br /> <br /> As he's navigating through her phone, he decides to do a little snooping and notices that she's been calling the same number a lot. There's no contact, but there's nothing but calls from this one number going back a couple of days. The most recent entry shows she called 6 times. Most of them seem to have gone answered, but the person seems to have picked them up occasionally. Derrik decides to commit the number to memory.<br /> <br /> Derrik mentions that his mom will get back to her at some point, offhandedly mentioning that it takes her a while to get back to him sometimes too. Which is absolutely not him understatedly expressing his anxiety at the fact that his mom has yet to text him back yet. Nope, no anxiety here. Derrik Thorpe, anxiety free since 1999.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat's the problem with being a busy working woman. But the alternative is just staying home and doing all the work around the house. Having the husband controlling the purse strings, so...&quot; - Mrs. Carver<br /> <br /> &quot;Wouldn't want that...&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Xeno: Are you being held hostage? Do you need help?<br /> Keni: It FEELS like it!</span><br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, you know what? we should have you over sometime. I think it would be lovely.&quot; - Mrs. C<br /> <br /> She mentions that her husband Jack is on a work trip in China, which Derrik thinks is actually really awesome. Mrs. Carver doesn't get the appeal, but notes that their house has \u201clacked a little bit of male presence&quot; and that it\u2019d be nice to have some for a change. But her excitement quickly melts into lamentation at the fact that she needs to pack up Jacob's dorm now that he's gone, setting off Derrik's well-mannered good boy instincts.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you need help packing something... I could help out.&quot; - Derrik, voice cracking.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh I couldn't possibly ask for that. It's too much.... But if you're sure.&quot; - Mrs. Carver, dropping that last sentence the second it looks like Derrik might back away.<br /> <br /> She mentions that she has a spare key to the room that she can give him. Her &quot;hot flashes&quot; are intensifying, which at this point everyone is taking as a sign that she wants a piece of Derrik.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">The cougar jokes were in full swing. Trust me, there are a lot of things in this chronicle that want a piece of Derrik. Mrs. Carver is not actually one of them. But her one true love is attention, so it's an easy mistake to make.</span><br /> <br /> Mrs. Carver seems curious about Derrik's &quot;friends&quot; in the back, though Derrik is not keen on being lumped in with them whatsoever. He also straight up tells her that Collin was Jacob's school project, which she figures is &quot;a psychology thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u201cAnthropology.\u201d \u2013 Her daughter<br /> <br /> They walk arm in arm to the back of the church, chatting about Elaine's new hobby, selling Korean skincare products. Mrs. Carver is thrilled at the idea and talks about her struggle finding authentic products in the Facebook groups she\u2019s in. Derrick says he\u2019ll put them in touch, but wants to get out of that conversation as soon as possible. He\u2019s grateful when they get to the back of the church and Mrs. Carver\u2019s attention is split between the three of them.<br /> <br /> Damian introduces himself and &quot;Collins&quot; and is finally corrected.<br /> <br /> &quot;I hope you can find solace in his memory.&quot; - Collin to Mrs. C.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thank you for that, Collin. I hope that now that he's gone, you can still continue your Dungeons and Dragons or whatever it is that you played together. Don't stop on his account.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Now, this is a moment I thought would be a bombshell but went completely unnoticed by anyone but Keni. Weeks later, we still sometimes bring up how Collin had no reaction whatsoever to the implication that Mrs. Carver knew about Collin from Jacob and that Jacob was somehow part of Collin's D&amp;D group without his knowledge. I would have called more attention to it, but I honestly thought that he was just keeping his cards close to the vest at first. It's okay, though, I'll have other opportunities to drop this piece of information and have Screwy freak out.</span><br /> <br /> After a bit of flirting between Mrs. Carver and Damian (Mrs. C: &quot;I think I had a boyfriend once named Damian. It was a long time ago.&quot; / Damian: &quot;Must have been a lucky man.&quot; / Mrs. C: &quot;Oh, stop.&quot;), she suggests they all help Derrik out with clearing out Jacob\u2019s stuff. She seems glad at the prospect of this horrible tragedy bringing people together. Unfortunately, she doesn't actually know which dorm is Jacob's or what room he was in. Damian texts his office group chat in the hopes that his assistant, Ollie, can help find that information for him. He texts back a buck-toothed nerd glasses thumbs up emoji, which Damian hates. Oddly, it seems that the message does not go through for Sarah, though he doesn't think much about it. As long as one person's on the case, it should be fine.<br /> <br /> Derrik still has his eyes on Sam and the priest, who are standing almost unusually still, facing away from the rest of them. He can feel the tension between the two of them, and whatever they're discussing, it's quite heated. But then Sam bumps the other man on the shoulder with the back of his fist and heads back in their direction, saying, \u201cGreat talking to you as always.&quot;<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Collin has run over to Abigail to ask about Jacob's dorm and room number. She seems confused about why he\u2019s interested in that given everything that\u2019s happened recently.<br /> <br /> \u201cDidn't you say you were sort of pen pals and it turned out you were his class project or something?&quot;<br /> <br /> Collin explains Mrs. Carver's request and she nods along, though she seems somewhat skeptical. After looking into it, she gets him the dorm name and specific room number. Collin, for some reason, decides to ask her if there's anything they should be on the lookout for when they get there. Surprised by the question, she thinks about it for a moment.<br /> <br /> &quot;Somebody at the home base said that they were missing their keys or something? Maybe if you find them you could send me a text.&quot; - Abigail<br /> <br /> She gives them a call, keeping her eyes on Collin the entire time. She tells the person on the other end that she\u2019s talking to a real sweet guy named Collin, explaining that they\u2019re at the funeral and that he\u2019s wondering what the keys look like. Yeah, the ones that are missing. She says that they think Jacob might have had them and that Collin\u2019s going to go looking for them on their behalf. The description she passes onto Collin is a set of brassy room keys on a square key ring. It\u2019s apparently some sort of hand-me-down. Collin thanks her for the info and heads back to the others to let them know what\u2019s up.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah, for fuck's sake.\u201d - Damian, texting Ollie to cancel his investigation.<br /> <br /> After a minute delay, he receives a selfie taken from above of Ollie holding a Pomeranian under his arm, giving a thumbs up.<br /> <br /> Ollie: Making progress!!!<br /> <br /> &quot;What do I pay these people for?&quot; - Damian, shaking his head.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">He's actually hard at work on a case about missing dogs, which is the funniest part of all this. At least one of his employees is a hard worker, but poor Ollie gets lumped in with Sarah because they\u2019re both Gen Z.</span><br /> <br /> Without warning, Mrs. Carver's eyes roll back in her head and she passes out, but not before Damian swoops in and catches her mid-fall. If she were conscious she'd probably even swoon in his arms and start planning a lovely summer wedding for the two of them. Luckily she\u2019s not mentally there to witness this act of heroism. Derrik pushes past Sam, who\u2019s returned from the front, and tries to examine Jacob\u2019s mother. She was saying she was hot before, and there could be a couple potential causes for a woman of her age to pass out all of a sudden. But a quick vital check helps him rule out anything serious like a heart attack. He can\u2019t be sure without a more thorough examination, but he figures it's most likely just the hot flashes or dehydration. At the very least, she's breathing normally and otherwise looks fine, aside from a little clamminess.<br /> <br /> From the vestibule, an authoritative voice nobody recognizes calls out to the group crowding around Mrs. Carver, asking them all to step aside. In jogs a fit Asian man in his mid- to late 20s in a cream shirt and denim jacket. He's got pink tinted sunglasses on his head, long styled bangs, and a sizable cross-body bag slung over his back. Together, he and Damian seat her down on the back pew, at which point her eyes flutter open and she blinks around in confusion at the sudden attention. Over the next few minutes, the new guy gets down on one knee and begins to take her vitals, producing a pulse oximeter, blood sugar kit, and even a pressure cuff and stethoscope from his bag. As he works, he and Mrs. Carver chat, and it becomes quickly apparent that they're relatively well-acquainted with one another. He seems slightly exasperated with her, though she doesn\u2019t seem to notice or acknowledge it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thank you, I'm so sorry, I didn't mean to cause a scene.&quot; - Mrs. Carver, which Collin immediately clock as being false.<br /> <br /> Once Mrs. Carver\u2019s condition is confirmed to be stable, people immediately begin bombarding the new guy with questions. He doesn't go to UCLA (which he finds to be a random thing to ask) and he's not actually a doctor like they all presume. It turns out he's a paramedic and has only recently come to be acquainted with the inimitable Mrs. Carver. She calls him &quot;Ray.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Go on, tell them the story of how we met.&quot; - Mrs. C, seemingly out of a desire to hear the story retold more than anything else.<br /> <br /> According to him, she passed out during brunch with a couple of her girlfriends a few days ago and he happened to be on the scene when they freaked out and tried to call an ambulance. After a cursory check, it turned out that she was fine physically. Mrs. Carver helpfully adds that she regaled him with the story of her son\u2019s passing, unironically using the the term 'knight in shining armor' to describe him at one point.<br /> <br /> &quot;And I told him, \u2018There's going to be a funeral and I absolutely need you to come. I will not take no for an answer. But only if you're comfortable with it, of course.\u2019&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Mrs. Carver, everyone.</span><br /> <br /> As they're introducing themselves to the new guy, Damian notes that he's here on behalf of someone who knew Jacob but \u201chad a falling out with him\u201d and so didn't want to show up in person. This is notably a different story than he's told Derrik or Collin at this point, but nobody brings it up or questions him about it and the new guy certainly doesn\u2019t have any reason to pry. Despite Mrs. Carver mentioning him by name earlier, Derrik asks for his name, suggesting that \u201cRay\u201d might have been a fake one.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why would I give her a fake name...? Wait, wait, so is Derrik your real name? Or is it a fake name that you're giving me?&quot; - Ray<br /> <br /> Derrik assures him that it's his real name, at which point the others exchange names as well. Ray suggests they stop by Five Guys to grab lunch since it's just down the street and nobody\u2019s had anything to eat yet. Derrik, only half paying attention, can\u2019t seem to find Sam anywhere. It seems he slipped away in the commotion earlier.<br /> <br /> As the others begin to make their way out, Collin decides to let his curiosity get the best of him and runs up to the altar to examine the floor where he'd seen the blood dripping earlier. The priest does not notice his greeting, or perhaps simply does not acknowledge it, instead focusing on the stained glass windows at the back with a look of deep contemplation on his face. Finding the spot on the floor where he saw the weird stuff with the Jesus statue before, he bends down and begins hurriedly patting at the ground to see if he can find any traces of blood. Unfortunately (or maybe fortunately) there is nary a mark or stain on the surface. As he rises, though, something very wrong occurs. He trips and tumbles into the statue, feeling a burning sensation across his arm and falling in a heap on the ground. He's not sure exactly what happened, but though the statue is unharmed, his sleeve ripped, and his arm bleeding from a gash across it like in the dream he\u2019d seen before.<br /> <br /> &quot;What are the two of you getting up to over there?&quot; - Ray, turning to look at Derrik behind him and Collin on the ground by the altar.<br /> <br /> &quot;Jesus hurt him, it looks like.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;That is certainly a sentence. Not sure if the Father will take kindly to this?&quot; - Ray<br /> <br /> But the priest does not respond whatsoever. It seems his contemplation is quite deep indeed.<br /> <br /> Both Ray and Derrik hurry over to examine Collin but curiously neither find anything to be wrong with him, at least physically. His sleeve is ripped, certainly, and stained red, but Collin bears no external injuries of note. Derrik hurriedly grabs him under the armpits and drags him away from the statue.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">I love when people choose Dramatic Failures and really weird things start happening during an Awakening scenario. Also, neither Xeno nor Screwy caught this in the moment, but Derrik's reaction to this situation is quite interesting here. Collin seems completely unharmed, so why <i>drag</i> him away from the statue?</span><br /> <br /> &quot;Where's the blood from?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;Maybe Jesus rubbed off on him while he was playing around back here?&quot; - Ray<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't really recommend it.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">This made me cackle for reasons that will make sense when you get to Derrik's backstory. It's really not what you think. Probably.</span><br /> <br /> As he's being dragged out of the church, Collin shouts a &quot;Thank you, padre&quot; to the very Irish-American priest, who slowly turns and nods once before returning his gaze to the wonders beyond the stained glass. Before exiting the large double doors, Derrik turns back as well, against his better judgment, and locks eyes with the priest. At just that moment, the sun slips out from behind a cloud outside, casting its light through the window and framing the priest with a golden aura. He opens his mouth to speak and Derrik immediately nopes out of there, completely refusing any attempt to understand exactly what the man had to say to him.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Unfortunate, really, but I didn't expect any different.</span><br /> <br /> Damian, meanwhile, has been waiting outside for the others for several minutes at this point after saying goodbye and doing the requisite flirting ritual required to sate Mrs. Carver\u2019s narcissism. When the others finally join him, he\u2019s lighting up a cigarette as he waits impatiently.<br /> <br /> \u201cJesus Christ.\u201d - Damian<br /> <br /> The group make their way across the street to Five Guys, Derrik avoiding the cracks on the sidewalk as Collin fails to text Dave and ask if he wants to come along. Find My Friends says that he's at UCLA for some reason, which concerns Collin greatly. But there\u2019s nothing he can do about the situation from where he is in Downtown LA. Derrik asks whether the man he\u2019s looking for is his boyfriend, to which Collin explains that he's his &quot;concierge.&quot; Everybody raises their eyes in confusion.<br /> <br /> Ray gets invited to the UCLA dorm room clearing, and upon further questioning, shares that he abandoned his dreams of being a doctor way back in college but went back to school to become a paramedic later on. He orders three burgers in addition to fries and a drink, virtually swallowing the last burger whole when he realizes everyone has long since finished eating and waiting on him. Derrik then turns to Collin.<br /> <br /> &quot;Let's go find your guy who's your concierge and not your boyfriend.\u201d<br /> <br /> Damian offers to drive people, especially since neither Collin nor Derrik have a ride. Ray seems to have come on a motorcycle and says he can always come pick up his bike later if they\u2019re all going to head over there together.<br /> <br /> &quot;By the way, Derrik. Is this yours?&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> Derrik looks up from the sidewalk curiously and Damian snaps a photo of him and Collin, sending it to Ollie over the work group chat. Derrik freaks out and starts swinging at Damian, though he completely misses the mark in his panic.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy oh my, is that what they teach you at law school now?&quot; - Damian, unconcerned.<br /> <br /> After some more jabs about Derrik's law knowledge or lack thereof (including one from Collin, surprisingly), Ray gets between him and Damian, hands outstretched, trying to diffuse the suddenly tense situation that he\u2019s found himself in.<br /> <br /> &quot;I feel like I'm missing so much context and I'm kinda reevaluating this whole going to clean out his room thing.&quot; - Ray<br /> <br /> Derrik steps away from the group to call his mom in a panic but gets a message that the number could not be reached. So he calls the only other person that he regularly interacts with, and she thankfully answers. The woman seems surprised to be receiving a call from him, especially at this time of day.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not relapsing or anything, it's not like that. There's just this PI guy that's randomly investigating me and I just wanted to call someone to tell them that IF I END UP DYING YOU KNOW WHAT HAPPENED.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you need me to call the police?&quot; - The woman<br /> <br /> Derrik says no, which confuses her greatly in light of his previous statement. After composing himself, Derrik apologizes for calling and explains that he's just freaked out because he can't find his mom, at which point the woman asks him to say yes if he needs her to call 911. He says no, she guides him through a breathing exercise, and the two of them have the most awkward end of a call that you can imagine. At the very least, Derrik shares his location with the woman, who seems to be his therapist.<br /> <br /> After everyone (mostly Derrik) is somewhat more calm, Ray ushers them to Damian\u2019s old Chevy Cruise before any new arguments can break out, and the group make their way across town to UCLA. The car reeks of smoke and is incredibly messy on the inside, which sets Derrik on edge, but Ray doesn't seem to be bothered.<br /> <br /> The buildings of UCLA are designed in the Romanesque style in pale creams and roses, with lush green lawns separating them. It's a massive campus, but thankfully 3 out of 4 members of the group are familiar with the campus (even if only two of them actually attended in person). As they\u2019re navigating the campus and figuring out the parking situation, they get into a conversation about school and studies, which gets side tracked by a conversation about Derrik\u2019s home state of South Dakota.<br /> <br /> &quot;What's the difference between North and South Dakota?&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> &quot;I believe one is below the other.&quot; - Ray, without skipping a beat.<br /> <br /> Derrik gives Collin a short intro to US history before he and Damian rib him about his &quot;fake&quot; cryptography degree. Trying to support Collin and his \u201cuseless\u201d degree, Ray points out that a large percentage of med school applicants are actually English majors, which Damian concedes is at least a real major, unlike art.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think this is an unsafe environment and I maybe need to go home.&quot; - Ray, revealing that he studied dance.<br /> <br /> Damian is confused why a dance major would go on to become a paramedic. It\u2019s a long story.<br /> <br /> Since it's the summer semester, there's not a lot of students around. They get into Jacob's dorm easily enough and make their way toward the room Abigail said was his. Just outside the door, as Damian is about to turn the key in the lock, Derrik hears voices inside. Pressing his ear against the door, he can make out two people talking, though he only understands one passing comment.<br /> <br /> &quot;Where is it? It's gotta be around here somewhere.&quot; - Voice 1<br /> <br /> Derrik immediately throws the door open. Inside, two individuals freeze in surprise. One of them is a girl just under six feet tall and on the muscular side. She's white with dirty blonde hair and looks like she could be a varsity athlete. Next to her is a Black guy of about five and a half feet with his hair buzzed short and a gangly but small frame. The two groups stare at each other for a long beat as wind blows through the open window behind the intruders.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, you got here first. You're here to help us?&quot; - Collin, trying a bluff.<br /> <br /> The boy steps forward, seeming to relax and fall for it. But the girl is not so easily fooled and puts her hand in front of him to stop as she looks between him and the others. Then, without warning, she turns and leaps out the window they seem to have entered from, slamming it shut and trapping her companion in there with the group. Damian takes out his phone and takes a picture of his face, which completely freaks him out. He throws up his hands, half pleading and trying to cover his face.<br /> <br /> &quot;Please please please, don't do that. I don't know what you're doing but don't do that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Damian sends the picture to the office group chat regardless, and the group begins trying to intimidate him, despite his best attempts to explain what's going on and beg for lenience. He says that if they just let him leave, they don't have to have any problems. When that doesn\u2019t work, he also suggests that he'll scream if they don't let him leave. That only makes our three protagonists laugh.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">This was one of those situations where the players\u2019 actions sucker punch you. I was shocked at the way this conversation went, thinking that none of the PCs would want to explain what was going on to a security guard, especially not one that came running because a student was screaming. But they seemed to think that being there on behalf of a deceased student's mom would give them the edge if it came down to it. They would be wrong in this case, but luckily did not have the opportunity to test that theory out. It did frustrate the heck out of the boy, though, who had figured he had a winning strategy only to find out his opponents thought he was stupid.</span><br /> <br /> As Derrik runs to the window to give chase to the girl, the disgruntled boy sticks out his foot, causing him to trip and faceplant into the wall. Realizing the world of hurt he is about to be in if Derrik catches him, he then makes a mad dash for the door, darting between Collin and Ray and trying to escape. Ray calls out that he's got him, but Derrik is furious and decides to give chase as well. By the window, Damian spies the girl making her way through the garden behind the dorm and heading around a corner at the far side. He decides to engage in a chase of his own, tossing the room key to Collin and instructing him to lock up. Naturally, the instruction is immediately forgotten.<br /> <br /> Collin spins around, looking around the room for clues now that he\u2019s on his own. It seems sparsely decorated and not very lived in. The desk is bare aside from a laptop and a polaroid camera next to it. The bookshelf beside it is crammed full of books aside from one section in the middle where there's a conspicuous gap. But the most notable thing Collin finds is the closet, in which all the clothes have been pushed to the sides to reveal a massive investigation board along the back wall that runs from side to side and floor to ceiling. It is covered in photos, printouts, and sticky notes connected with pins and red tape. Among the sea of notes, he finds a work photo of Damian and accompanying office picture, blurry photos of Derrik entering his Aston Martin, and a series of properties located around the country connected to a blurry webcam photo of his own face. <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">And that's where we ended the session! I really liked the dramatic end point, though it always feels like we need one more hour. Time just goes by so fast when you\u2019re having fun, and there's only so much you can get done in a three hour session, even with only three players. But we managed to finally escape the church and learn a great deal about Jacob and his situation. Like the fact that he was at some point spying on the group. But for what purpose? And how did he gain access to Collin's webcam?<br /> <br /> Like I said last time, you really can never predict exactly what the PCs will do and what will catch their interest. With all the NPCs at the church, there were a ton of avenues of investigation open to the characters. But because they only talked to Abigail and Mrs. Carver, his room was the only obvious choice. If they\u2019d asked around or learned some more, this investigation board would likely make a little more sense than it does, but the drama of them finding the board and realizing that Jacob might be a stalker was certainly delicious. Even better, it\u2019s all contextless since they haven\u2019t really picked up many clues about Jacob thus far. I can't wait to see what sort of conclusions they end up jumping to next session as they analyze the information he\u2019s gathered.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T18:03:25-07:00","id":1554751,"title":"","content":"Great start!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T18:07:07-07:00","id":1554752,"title":"","content":"Thank you! We've been having a lot of fun so far.<br /> <br /> The next writeup should be dropping soon, just need a Mod to approve it (I fought too much with the formatting and the spam filter didn't like it). The third writeup will drop tomorrow night, and from there I'll be releasing these weekly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T08:20:15-07:00","id":1554773,"title":"","content":"I've seen your Actual Play over at RPG.net. I enjoyed it so much, I already shared it at the Discord I frequent. I had most fun with the awkward humor, and how rich in personality all the NPCs are. I'm eagerly waiting for more!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T11:31:33-07:00","id":1554782,"title":"","content":"I'm thrilled that you're enjoying TEC and I appreciate you sharing it! If you love the awkward humor and NPC work, you're going to have a lot of fun with the recaps that are coming up!<br /> <br /> I'd definitely recommend reading it here since the edit feature is much more forgiving! And speaking of, the next section of the story should drop sometime today. Hope you enjoy what we've got cooked up for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T18:05:35-07:00","id":1554803,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">A great start for the story, I'm looking forward to the next chapter. Collin is so goal oriented and earnest that he sounds crazy to non-mages, Damian is really methodical yet intense and Derrik is instinctively compelled to keep going despite being terrified. Damian just meeting Derrick by going full detective mode was really unexpected, but lead to a memorable first impression.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Based on their characterization so far, I am guessing Collin will become an Acanthus Guardian of the Veil, Damian will be a Mastigos of the Adamantine Arrow and Derrik an Obrimos of the Silver Ladder.</div></div> </div> </div></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">I wouldn't be surprised if the Bearers of the Sacred Heart were a Cryptopoly, the 5 black roses (symbols of rebirth, transformation and new begginings) represent the Watchtowers and the thorny bush the Fallen World. Doubly so because Dr Devi was probably reading High Speech and the priest might have flared his Nimbus with that divine light effect. If so, it's a pretty sneaky bit of foreshadowing, very cool.</span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">I really liked your policy on Dramatic Failures, giving a way for attentive players to keep the momentum.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T22:49:12-07:00","id":1554829,"title":"","content":"<br /> Glad to have you along for the ride!<br /> <br /> Collin really fits the stereotypical image of a mage, utterly obsessive and single-minded when it comes to pursuing his goals. Damian's intensity and matter-of-factness makes for a nice contrast (and he's the perfect straight man in their comedic duo), but as you'll increasingly see in future writeups, he's actually a total softie underneath that gruff exterior. And Derrik is eternally that friend in the horror movie who keeps telling everyone to leave but gets dragged along because no one will listen and he doesn't have the heart to abandon them.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Great predictions! We're currently at a point in the story where their paths have been revealed and they're starting to learn about and consider the orders, and you've hit the nail on the head with some of these, particularly the Paths. The orders are still up in the air, but their current leanings might surprise you.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Very interesting read on the symbolism of the roses and the truth behind the events of the &quot;funeral.&quot; Some of this will come up later in a big way so I can't confirm or deny most of it, but I will say that it's definitely High Speech she's reading.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> On that note, I'll be sharing the next writeup in a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T00:00:05-07:00","id":1554831,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>\u2bcc</b> <b>0.2 | Murder Wall</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u201cHumankind has not woven the web of life. We are but one thread within it. Whatever we do to the web, we do to ourselves. All things are bound together. All things connect.\u201d \u2014 Chief Seattle</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u2bcc \u2bce \u2bcc</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">This was a pretty big session in terms of revelations after two very discussion-heavy ones. Notably, I'd had the entire Mystery of the first Chapter planned out for over a month at this point. With all the extra free time, I had the opportunity to go over it again and again, tweaking and refining it. Ending the previous session right at the discovery of the wall in particular gave me a ton of time to reflect on it and how I wanted to handle this part of the investigation. The PCs discovering the wall without any helpful context meant that a lot of time was spent putting pieces together and hypothesizing, but I suppose it\u2019s okay to have a lull in the action every once in a while so that people can get their bearings and try and make sense of things.</span><br /> <br /> Collin begins by calling up his buddy in the tech sector, who we learn works in cybersecurity and manages most of Collin's security needs. Collin asks how easy it would be for someone to hack into his computer, which makes his friend laugh. He soon realizes that Collin is serious, though, and takes a break from his bench press to consider the hypothetical. According to him, it really shouldn\u2019t be possible. As they\u2019re chatting, Collin spots an obituary for his long-dead parents on the \u201cmurder wall\u201d and, frustrated that someone has intel on him, asks Steve if there's a program he could send over to crack this guy's password. Steve asks for 15 minutes to run home.<br /> <br /> As Collin hangs up, five bells ring in succession, marking it as 5:00 p.m. He turns his attention to the open space right in the middle of Jacob's bookshelf. All around it are books on anthropology, mainly concerning myths. They've all got markings from the Anthropology Department library here at UCLA and seem to have been recently checked out. He assumes that the missing book(s) must be from the library as well, based on the way the shelf is organized, but there's no way to tell exactly what it might be a book on. Looking back at the murder well, there are noticeable empty spaces as well, though it's hard to tell whether they just hadn't been filled up yet or whether Jacob or someone else had removed what was there previously. Either way, Collin switches focus again to try and take in the room in its totality and see if he can spot anything else amiss. The clock on the wall ticks in the background.<br /> <br /> Overall, the dorm room feels not very lived in. There are no notebooks or folders, papers for class, or any other marks of a student aside from the laptop on the desk. As his search for a journal of some kind turns up nothing, he becomes aware of a second ticking noise, out of sync with that of the clock. Turning, he finds none other than Sam Bishop, the blond man in the impeccable blue suit from the funeral, lounging on the bed. He\u2019s propped up on one elbow, face in hand, sucking on a chocolate Tootsie Pop. When Collin sputters in confusion, he mentions that the door is open.<br /> <br /> Figuring that the bed might be a good hiding place, Collin decides he wants to flip the mattress, so Sam hops off and gives him some space. Though the bed itself contains nothing of interest, peeking out from the slats underneath is something round, vaguely coin-shaped. It's either brass or bronze and just a bit smaller than Collin's palm. As he examines the medallion, he notes strange runic symbols carved along the edge. One side bears a proud-looking man in Roman attire with a spear in hand and laurels in his hair. The other simply depicts a round shield.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm assuming that's very tasty.&quot; - Collin, distracted by the loud smacking sounds of Sam sucking on his candy of choice.<br /> <br /> The man politely offers him one, which he takes before instructing Sam to go take a look in the closet. Sam gives a shrug, says, \u201cSure,\u201d and walks on in.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">This is one of those situations that makes Keni think Collin has \u201cmain character energy.\u201d You meet a strange man at a funeral for a guy who was sort of your pen-pal but not quite. He disappears without a word, but then shows up lounging around in the guy's bed after you've arranged to clear out his room hours later. Despite the initial surprise, Collin does not ask any follow up questions about Sam's goals or intentions. Instead, he takes it on the chin and asks him to investigate the closet despite neither of them acknowledging what the other is doing here. Sam, of course, goes along with it. Sure hope he's not actually involved in this or some kind of antagonist working against the PCs or anything, because Collin's giving him the best possible opportunity to mess with all the evidence nobody's actually fully examined yet.</span><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Derrik is in the midst of a chase sequence. His quarry is ducking through the hallways, hoping to sneak around and use his better knowledge of the area to escape capture. Derrik falls behind at several points, though Ray's surprisingly sharp senses and athleticism allow him to keep on the trail. When they chase him out of a stairwell onto the third floor of the dorm, the boy tries a different tactic, calling out to the passerby and saying that there\u2019s crazy people running through the halls back there. Ray responds with an appeal of his own, projecting his voice down the hallway and insisting that his quarry is a danger to himself and others.<br /> <br /> This does not work the way he expects it to, as his tone of voice and volume set the students on edge, giving the guy a chance to escape. Derrik bolts after him, leaving Ray and the other students behind. His athletic background starts to shine here as the other boy has to stop to take a breather, and the next thing Derrik knows he's turned a corner and found his quarry backed into a dead end, clutching his head from where he banged it on the frame of the stairwell door during the chase.<br /> <br /> &quot;Doesn't feel so fucking good, does it?&quot; Derrik growls, and the lights overhead begin to flicker.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why couldn't you have just stayed still for a second and handled this LIKE A MAN?&quot;<br /> <br /> The light above the other guy shatters and he whimpers, covering his head to protect himself. Derrik, despite his concern, pretends not to have noticed this.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're gonna come with me and you're gonna answer everything. Do you understand?&quot;<br /> <br /> Another light explodes closer to the other guy. Derrik mumbles something about the wiring. The poor guy, looking apprehensive as all hell, steps closer and Derrik grabs his hand. But before he can celebrate, he hears the sound of footsteps approaching from the corner they just turned down.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Damian is also in the midst of a chase, and he has a significant disadvantage compared to Derrik. For starters, he's all on his own. On top of that, she looks to be a competitive runner or at least an athlete of some sort. As he rounds the corner to follow her, the sun passes behind a cloud above and the entire area suddenly dims.<br /> <br /> Students are milling about as they come back from class, which must have just let out. Damian figures it's better to work smarter than harder, using his somewhat out of date knowledge of the campus and basic geometry to compensate for his lack of track and field experience. He calls out to people nearby, saying that she's a thief that broke into one of the dorms, and it surprisingly works at first. Two guys move to intercept her, but then she says something that Damian can't quite make out but is probably about him being a creepy man, and they back off, figuring the situation is much too complicated to be worth sticking their noses into. The chase extends to the edge of campus and the girl keeps running, heading down a series of side streets and making her way toward an alley. Seeing his opportunity, Damian goes for a diving tackle and knocks her to the ground, the two of them eventually rolling to a stop.<br /> <br /> &quot;This is a citizen's arrest. You can either talk to me or you're going to the police station. And it's going in your record.&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> She's lying face down, somewhat winded, her dirty blonde hair a mess as it falls over his face. To his confusion and slight concern, he can see puffs of vapor coming from her nose, as if she were breathing out in the middle of Winter. The girl fixes him with a glare, slowly rising to her feet. But Damian pulls her arms back in a lock, forcing her to her feet. She growls in response, spitting at the ground angrily.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, come on, really?&quot; - Damian<br /> <br /> She makes a guttural noise in her throat by way of response, but goes along with him as he leads her out of the alleyway.<br /> <br /> It's at that point that he realizes that something really strange is going on. The sky above is gray and hazy, with no sign of the sun. The alleyway doesn't lead into the streets like he expected it to, but rather into another long alleyway that itself branches off into more branching paths in the distance. The walls all around are dingy and covered in filth, and a tall, tower-like structure made of iron curved into hook-like shapes looms far in the distance. Damian closes his eyes and shakes his head to clear this weird hallucination. When he opens them again, he realizes that the girl in front of him is, in fact, not a girl at all. As the thing turns to him, his nose is filled with the fetid musk of a wild beast as he makes eye contact with the face of a bull, its hot breath misting in the air as it gives him a derisive snort.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Xeno: You're telling me Collin sees bleeding Jesus and I see a goddamn minotaur?<br /> Yeah, buddy. Unfortunately that's exactly what I'm telling you.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> Back in the hallway, Derrik peeks around the corner. The individual making his way over to him is tall, with dusky skin and hair that falls to his shoulders and looks a little messy, as if he's run a hand through it and just left it like that. There's an almost unnatural stillness to him, like he's an anthropomorphized wall rather than a person. To his great discomfort and concern, Derrik recognizes him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"372\" height=\"481\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/3GGJwav.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/3GGJwav.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/3GGJwav.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;What...? Why are you here?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> The man blinks once, slowly, before replying.<br /> <br /> &quot;Business.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, me too. So if you'll excuse me, I have places to go and people to return to.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> But the man doesn't seem very keen on letting Derrik leave with his quarry. Rather, he insists on taking &quot;that one&quot; off his hands. Derrik has no idea what he wants with the guy, but he isn't about to just back down. In the course of the conversation, it comes out that the man's name is Jericho. Derrik expects there to be others with him, but thankfully Jericho seems to be operating alone today. He\u2019s exceedingly calm and collected with a bit of mild curiosity on his expression, in stark contrast to Derrik\u2019s rocketing anxiety and panic. He makes a point that Derrik could very well just leave at any time and Jericho will stop bothering him. But he's definitely taking the boy with him.<br /> <br /> &quot;Move aside, Jericho.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> Jericho, keeping his eyes on Derrik, steps backward a few paces and then one step over so that he's right in the center of the hallway, blocking progress. He shakes his head no. So Derrik turns to the guy he's been dragging along, trying to get as much information as he can at the moment.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why were you in Jacob's room? What were the two of you doing in there?&quot;<br /> <br /> The guy stutters as he searches for the right words. &quot;I.... was just doing what she said. She said she needed someone who knew the place, and I used to live in here, so I came along...&quot;<br /> <br /> After a few seconds, he adds, &quot;She was looking for some keys.&quot;<br /> <br /> After getting his assurance that that's the whole story, Derrik tells him to get behind him and steps in front, as if to protect him with his body. Jericho watches the two of them silently as the boy introduces himself as Brian Williams.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't really know what the situation is, but do you know why this... person would need to talk to you? Do you know each other?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> Brian looks up at Jericho and does not respond, at least until Derrik tightens his grip on his wrist, causing him to whimper in pain. Derrik asks his question again.<br /> <br /> &quot;Maybe... I've seen him before,&quot; Brian murmurs.<br /> <br /> Jericho is even more tight-lipped about what he\u2019s doing here, just repeating \u201cbusiness.\u201d<br /> <br /> &quot;What fucking business do you guys have other than doing drugs... and ruining people's lives?&quot;<br /> <br /> Jericho just shrugs.<br /> <br /> &quot;Jericho, just let us pass. I don't want to do this.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> At long last, Jericho seems to have made a decision about what to do. He steps toward Derrik and Brian, and just at that moment someone else calls out to the three of them from the other end of the hall. Sam Bishop struts over to them casually, one hand in his pocket and the other playing with the Tootsie Pop in his mouth.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm gonna need all of you to stop.&quot; - Sam<br /> <br /> Derrik experiences a rush of emotions, cycling through relief, joy, confusion, and concern in rapid succession: &quot;Oh, Sam! Wait, Sam? What the fuck are you doing here?&quot;<br /> <br /> Jericho slowly turns to look over his shoulder. Derrik tries to dodge around him and escape with Brian, but the other man notices and Derrik tenses up at the intense eye contact. His legs get tangled up in Brian's and the pair fall to the floor, landing in a pile of limbs right in front of Jericho.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">One thing I can always count on is my lovely players choosing to Dramatically Fail even when their characters desperately want to succeed.</span><br /> <br /> As he looks up at Jericho, Derrik realizes that Sam has managed to close the distance between him and the group without anyone noticing his approach. As he tugs at the bottom of his suit jacket, Derrik's attention is immediately drawn to the gun holstered by his waist. &quot;Wait wait wait!&quot; he shouts.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am going to need all of you to stand down.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;All?&quot; Derrik asks, noticing the intense eye contact Jericho is making with Sam. &quot;Don't.. Don't shoot him,&quot; he begs. &quot;Don't shoot any of us.&quot; Sam doesn't dignify that with a response. Instead, he says, &quot;I'm going to need to take these two in as part of an investigation. Sam Bishop, FBI.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, fuck.&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> Derrik steps in front of Brian, still protecting him, but his eyes are the size of saucers. He's clearly acting on pure instinct at this point. &quot;Can I call someone first?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You can try,&quot; Sam replies, nonchalant as ever.<br /> <br /> &quot;I was asking for permission, please.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sam shrugs. &quot;I mean, do what you want.&quot;<br /> <br /> Derrik looks back at Jericho, face even paler than usual. He sees Jericho retreating for the first time he can recall, his eyes locked on Sam, unblinking. &quot;Do you two know each other?&quot; he asks, getting increasingly worked up at the strange web of connections he\u2019s gotten tied up in. &quot;Well,&quot; Sam shoots back, &quot;I just introduced myself.... Don't you have a call to make? We're on bureau time.&quot;<br /> <br /> Derrik pulls out his burner phone and tries and fails to call his mom, getting a message that the number has been disconnected. Instead, he calls to mind the number he saw listed repeatedly on Mrs. Carver's phone at the funeral. After three rings, the owner picks up\u2014and it\u2019s Ray.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm getting arrested by Sam,&quot; Derrik says, which completely goes over Ray's head as he\u2019s never met the guy. He briefly explains the context, apologizes, and says that Sam's about to take him in. Ray says he's on his way and hangs up before Derrik can communicate that Sam's got a gun on him. But when Derrik offers up his wrists in surrender, Sam just shakes his head.<br /> <br /> &quot;We don't have to do that. We're in the middle of school, so... it's probably fine. Besides, neither of you are going to run, right?&quot; He smiles in a totally non-threatening manner.<br /> <br /> Derrik glances at the gun and shakes his head no before giving Brian a hand up. When he glances back to Jericho, there is no sign of him whatsoever. And when he looks back at Sam, there's a strange golden outline around him, like in a point-and-click video game when you're hovering over a Key Item. He's a little concerned, but pulls a Derrik and decides to ignore it.<br /> <br /> &quot;So... what now?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well,&quot; Sam says, looking around, &quot;It looks like we're alone so... you can do whatever you want.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...What? What? What!?!?! So you're not arresting us?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh. Are you actually FBI?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh...&quot;<br /> <br /> Derrik bends over double and begins to heave as the tension pours out of his body. Before long, he's back to his normal prickly self. &quot;What the fuck was that? Actually, no. No, I don't wanna know. Don't care.&quot; Sam just shrugs. &quot;Cool, that kinda makes things easier for me. So... I've kinda got some places to go... but I'll catch you around.&quot;<br /> <br /> When Derrik asks how to contact him, he says that Derrik's got his number, gives him a little wave, and then walks around the corner that Jericho mysteriously backed himself into and vanished from earlier. Certain it's a dead end, Derrik peers around the corner to find it empty yet again. He hurriedly assures himself that he does not care and does not want to know what any of that is about. Turning back to speak to Brian, he finds the hallway empty and hears the sound of a door slamming in the distance. It would seem that everyone's vanishing on him today.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> In the alleyway outside UCLA, Damian is hit with the musky, pungent odor of a wild animal. It's an acrid, sour smell that seems to radiate from the beast. Looking down at its body, it looks like that of a muscular girl, but as he watches, her musculature begins to stretch and expand, swelling and tearing apart until the girl he was chasing is a 6 foot 5 muscled minotaur. Damian does the only logical thing in the situation and whips out his phone, taking as many pictures as he can of the monstrosity in front of him. Then he takes off running. Unfortunately, the girl was faster than him back when she was human. Now that she's a giant predator with a stride that's easily twice his, he's got no chance. The last thing he remembers is being tackled from behind with the force of a truck, his body hitting the grimy metal of the walls of the alleyway before everything fades to black.<br /> <br /> Back in Jacob's room, Collin receives an email with the brute force program and calls his friend back to ask how it works. Steve tells him that he just has to load it onto a USB, plug it in, and it'll do all the heavy lifting for him. How long it takes will depend on the strength of the password, but it should be at least a couple minutes. Collin confirms that Steve's \u201con for next Thursday\u201d and Steve warns him to stay out of trouble before Collin ends the call.<br /> <br /> It takes 20 minutes to break in, but Steve's program does the job. As Collin logs in, Steam, Discord, and Google Chrome all pop up. He begins to examine the various apps that Jacob used, looking for the most recent modified files. In his documents he sees titles for recent school projects, mostly involving folklore, mythology, mirages, and sleepwalking. In terms of his search history, his most recent activity seems to have been a series of comments on Reddit. Collin notes that his avatar is the default, his username the same randomly generated string that you get when you create an account. He's never made any posts of his own, only comments, and they're exclusively on the subreddit WeirdButTrueLA. According to the description, it's a sub for documenting weird or unexplainable happenings in the city. It seems to mostly be collections of screenshots or short stories describing personal experiences.<br /> <br /> From Jacob's comment history, it seems that he's been reaching out to people and asking to DM them for more information. His chat history shows that he chatted with a couple of them, introducing himself as a grad student looking to set up interviews. His earliest comment is about a year old and the most recent is in December of 2024. Oddly, the user, remakingK, has no comment or post history and seems to have contacted Jacob rather than the other way around. The message just has a Discord handle, the same as his reddit username. When Collin goes to Discord to check, he notes that Jacob has no servers and exactly one friend: remakingK. Their chat history has only one message in it from this mysterious redditor: &quot;The person you're looking for can be found here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Attached to the message is a link to the Google Maps page for Collin's home address.<br /> <br /> This, notably, freaks him out. He begins going through various programs on the laptop trying to figure out if there's any hacking software installed.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">At this point, Collin is still working under the assumption that Jacob is some kind of master hacker who has cut through all the layers of his security, broken into his computer, and taken a picture of him using his webcam for his murder wall. But if we look at the evidence, this message history seems to imply that Jacob didn't even know where he lived or who he was until about 8 months ago. He definitely has stalker energy, and it does seem like he was looking for Collin in some form, but this remakingK individual was the one to point him in the right direction. This, combined with Mrs. Carver specifically telling Collin that she hoped he wouldn't let what happened get in the way of D&amp;D, suggests a far more likely explanation for how he got that webcam picture, don't you think?</span><br /> <br /> Collin decides to change Jacob's laptop password to prevent anyone else from getting in. But as he's typing in the new password, he sees strange symbols like those on the edge of the medallion appearing instead of letters. The keys on the keyboard appear to be shifting into that shape as well, and when he looks at a book on the shelf, its silver title mutates before his eyes. It turns out that that is the limit of weirdness Collin can tolerate and he leaves, but not before snapping a couple pictures of the investigation board (which he has lovingly called the murder wall). It is at this point, as he's locking the door behind him, that he hears the ringing of 5 bells to signal that it is now 5 o'clock. This is definitely the second time he's heard those bells now, which only serves to freak him out even more.<br /> <br /> Just then, Ray and Derrik return from the third floor to receive a word vomited, context-less string of events from Collin of what just transpired. What's worse, Collin will not under any circumstances go back into the room. He's freaked out and keeps saying that it's not a good place.<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you okay?&quot; - Ray<br /> <br /> &quot;No!&quot; - Collin<br /> <br /> He explains that he broke into Jacob's laptop and found a lot of weird stuff, which Derrik thinks is crossing the line. &quot;He had a picture of me on this murder wall!&quot; Collin replies defensively. This, of course, doesn\u2019t make any sense to Derrik, and he turns to Ray.<br /> <br /> &quot;Is it just me or does he just say things all the time that he expects us to understand?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I kind of think all of you do that. But it might just be because I joined late.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">He's right. Derrik gets on Collin's case, but both of them say the craziest things sometime with no context. Like, &quot;Hey, I'm in the middle of being arrested by Sam (who you don't know). Oh, he was at the funeral. He's FBI,&quot; followed by a distinct lack of FBI or signs of arrest when you meet back up.</span><br /> <br /> As they make their way into the room, they find Damian lying unconscious in Jacob's bed, tucked in by some kind soul. Collin, still outside, emphatically points out that he was not in there when he left.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Damian is floating in the void, but at the edge of his consciousness he can hear the sound of a lock being jiggled and the telltale sounds of someone trying to open a door. There's a grunt of frustration, maybe because of a stuck key, before a familiar masculine voice says, &quot;Finally.&quot; He smells Trout Piccata, tasting capers briefly on his tongue before waking up.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Both Keni and Xeno began screaming in disgust at the concept of tasting capers. Which is completely fair, but I'm just going off of what was written in the backstory! Later I learned that Xeno had forgotten about a particular experience that he'd written, leading to his surprise and confusion at this bit. When he realized what it was, he was like, &quot;Oh.... Oh.&quot; Because it was definitely something big. We'll get there eventually.</span><br /> <br /> He's feeling queasy and has a pounding headache, which isn't helped by the fact that his vision is swimming. Derrik has a kind of blue aura radiating around him, as does Collin, though his is yellow. Strangely, Ray does not seem to have any particular aura.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Xeno: &quot;It's because he's not chosen. Maybe he's not real?&quot;<br /> Well, he\u2019s certainly not Ray-el.</span><br /> <br /> Damian refuses all attempts to check his vitals or make sure he's okay. Strangely, though he feels awful, there are no bruises anywhere on his body. He rationalizes his recent experiences as a weird hallucination and figures that the girl must have hit him or something. At this point, Ray starts looking at the other three with worry. It seems like they've all developed strange behaviors in a very short span of time.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">I mean, imagine. Supposed FBI arrests that didn't go anywhere. Hearing things that don't make sense. Claiming that the unconscious person in bed was not there when you left the room 30 seconds ago and the window is locked. Insisting you were chasing someone and then woke up lying in bed with no recollection of how you got there. It\u2019s all concerning behavior.</span><br /> <br /> While his attention is turned away from Damian, Derrik notices the &quot;murder wall&quot; and notices a picture of a heavy iron key, the head crafted to look like a skeleton with blue gemstones glittering in its eye sockets. Derrik snaps a picture of it. That's when he sees the photos of himself and freezes. Despite everything, he's oddly calm about the situation.<br /> <br /> Damian, meanwhile, is looking for alcohol and drugs in the apartment since Abigail mentioned him &quot;going hard&quot; at the party and the toxicology report had said that he likely overdosed. But there are no bottles or drug paraphernalia around, and the minifridge is completely empty. It does not seem like the room of someone who was into the party scene. He joins Derrik at the murder wall and immediately notices a map of Union Station. Amtrak Baggage Services is circled in red and there's a receipt pinned to it dated July 31st, the day before Jacob's birthday (and the day he died). It appears that he had stored something there.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm glad you're not on here.&quot; - Derrik, to Ray<br /> <br /> &quot;I wouldn't expect to be. I mean, I barely knew the family.&quot; - Ray, spoken like an NPC out of his depth.<br /> <br /> Collin in Derrik get into a heated argument about him coming inside, which culminates in Derrik telling him to either come in or leave and not come back.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am doing this under duress.&quot; - Collin, taking a single step inside as Derrik locks the door.<br /> <br /> The PCs take some time to review the murder wall and spin theories about what exactly is going on. Derrik says he feels like cars have been following him for long periods of his life and that this makes him feel vindicated. He admits that he knew Jacob when they were kids but barely remembered him, and didn't even know his name until the funeral. He wants to know the name of Damian's employer because he feels like they might be out to try and kidnap him or something. Unfortunately, Damian has no idea who it is that employed him to look into Jacob. His top suspects were the Carver family and Sam, who he'd spotted scoping out the crowd during the funeral.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Collin shows the medallion to the others. Damian picks out that it's relatively new but effort was put into making it appear like an antique. From what he can tell, the medallion is likely some kind of badge or signifier of some sort. Perhaps a collector's item? He reasons that it likely has some kind of significance within some small, esoteric group, though he has no idea what that group might be.<br /> <br /> Collin checks his tracking app and notices Dave is on the highway heading back in the direction of the church. He gives him a ring, but gets little out of him other than a quick, &quot;Hey boss&quot; before loud sirens in the background drown him out. He asks what Dave's up to, but his voice is glitchy on the other end and the call ends up dropping. Anxious, Collin checks the news and finds out that there was a 2 car collision on the freeway just now, which must have been the source of the sirens. He sends Dave a couple texts, but they go undelivered.<br /> <br /> At about this time, Ray waves his phone at everyone. A quick search for Elias pulled up Elias Ren, a Teaching Assistant in the Anthropology Department at UCLA. The picture he shows everyone is of a skinny Asian man with circular glasses, hair in a small ponytail with an undercut, and preppy clothes. He's got a dark academia vibe and looks identical to the man Derrik, Collin, and Damian saw on the screensaver of Jacob's laptop. Having found their next lead, the four of them head out to the Anthropology building, deciding to split up. Damian and Collin go to check out the library while Derrik and Ray look for Elias's office.<br /> <br /> The first thing Damian and Collin notice is that there are 2 security guards conspicuously posted outside the library. They remember that Brian Williams had said something about security and the library right before the chase. But neither guard seems particularly interested in them as they enter. The Anthropology Department's library is on the smaller side. Perhaps because of summer session, there's only one person out in the stacks and one librarian behind the counter, a short woman with a bob and glasses. Damian introduces himself, and the second he says the word &quot;investigation,&quot; she lights up and says that he must be here about the missing book. She tells him that she's already explained all she knows to the administration, but that she's willing to answer any questions that he might have. As far as she's aware, there's never been a case of theft from this library before, and it was such an obscure book that she can't understand why someone would steal it.<br /> <br /> Damian, who was originally going to ask about Jacob, switches gears immediately and begins to inquire about the book. She informs him that the book itself had no title on the spine or cover, but it was old and bore signs of extensive use. It came from a collection of books donated by former alumni and people with ties to the university, and it seemed to be written in some kind of &quot;very strange hieroglyphics&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> &quot;Jacob and I spent so much time pondering what it could mean.&quot; - Librarian<br /> <br /> Damian approximates the size of the missing book from Jacob's room with his fingers and the librarian says that's the right size. When Collin shows her the medallion, she confirms that the strange hieroglyphs looked just like those runes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Perhaps you should talk to Elias. He was the one who pointed it out to me in the first place.&quot; - Librarian<br /> <br /> Before they leave, they ask her about any other books Jacob might have been interested in. The librarian, who clearly does not know Jacob's fate, says there might have been a project last year for one of Elias's class to do with urban legends, but that was a long time ago. From what she remembers, he had checked out books on dreams and sleepwalking, as well as one about mirages. She mentions that she hasn't seen him in weeks, and the two PCs decide it's better to let someone else break the news to her.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Derrik and Ray make their way through the maze of hallways in the Anthropology department, finally arriving at a hallway deep in the heart of the building. At the far end is a small, nondescript door with the name Elias Ren written in chalk. There's a poster with two clocks in it, labelled Time Out and Time In. Based on the hands of the clock, it looks like Elias left 5 or so minutes ago and plans to be back in 25 minutes. But Derrik notices there's light on under the door and he can't make out any sounds from inside the room. Ray says it can't hurt to take a peek, so the two of them make their way inside.<br /> <br /> It's a small, cozy office space that is conspicuously clean. Elias is clearly something of a neat freak. There's a desk and three chairs, a mobile blackboard covered in papers, maps, and writing. He's got neat stacks of to-be graded papers on the desk, a laptop, and a satchel hanging from behind his chair. A candle is burning on his desk and it smells faintly of lavender.<br /> <br /> Derrik and Ray perform a quick search and almost immediately hit the payload.<br /> <br /> Derrik finds a book called &quot;The City of Angels&quot; and a few others on funerary practices and burial rites in the satchel. He takes a few pictures, but then notices the chalkboard has a map of the US with large red dots at particular spots across the country. On top of it is a map of missing persons cases, each one represented by dots. For some reason, the missing persons cases form clusters that match the areas of interest on the first map. More concerning for Derrik is the fact that Elias or someone else has drawn biblically accurate angels on the board. As Ray leans on it, it flips over and reveals something else. There are a series of symbols that look just like the ones on the medallion Collin found in Jacob's room. Under them is a quatrain.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Gather the Keys<br /> Guard them and Wait<br /> Only their Union<br /> Will Open The Gate</span><br /> <br /> Derrik immediately pulls out his phone and starts capturing evidence. He tells Ray that he should probably flip it back around and he goes to do just that. It is at that moment that the boys hear the sound of a throat clearing and turn to see none other than Elias Ren standing with his arms crossed at the door. He hasn't shaved in days, bears noticeable dark circles under his eyes, and his right arm is bandaged from his elbow to his fingertips. His face is wet, as if he just splashed water on it.<br /> <br /> &quot;...And what exactly are you doing in here?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">Elias has a British accent, but at times it's rather faint or imperceptible.</span><br /> <br /> &quot;Uh.... Coming to meet you?&quot; - Derrik<br /> <br /> Elias raises an eyebrow at that. &quot;I see,&quot; he says as he steps inside the office, closes the door behind him, and turns the lock.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">And that's the end of Chapter 3! Honestly, there's nothing quite like listening to the players scream in anxiety after I end on a cliffhanger. It's almost enough to stave off the sadness of having to wait an entire week for more. 3.5 hours just isn't enough.<br /> <br /> Overall, I'd say that I'm pretty satisfied with how this chapter went. The struggle of the Storyteller is wondering how things look from the perspective of the players and hoping that they don't feel too lost or out of their depth. But I've got great players who roll with the punches and never fail to throw curveballs my way. This session they really started using the group whiteboard to take notes, which fills me with joy and pride. I'm the kind of player that puts together a 100 page theory document when I'm a player in a mystery game, so it's fun to see the kinds of connections they make and the things they focus on. Now, the players don't know that they're in a Mage: the Awakening game, but you all do. So I'm wondering what people think so far.<br /> <br /> What's up with Jacob Carver? What do the strange things they're experiencing mean? How about that ominous poem on the whiteboard? Points and a NPC named after you for anyone who can correctly guess what's going on or what I have planned.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T19:11:04-07:00","id":1554907,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Based on what we saw so far, this is my wild guess:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The use of angels, the Abyssal flood, the religious motifs, the session start quote about weaving. The Keys, whatever they are, hold the power of binding and loosing. The Gate in the poem is The Gate, the Exarch of the Abyss, the Keys would allow someone to open or close it. Since that could lead to the Abyss flooding into reality, there might be some Scelestus shenanigans afoot. </div></div> </div> </div></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jacob Carver had his history rewritten, the photo &quot;never taken&quot; is an item preserved from the original timeline via </span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Shield of Chronos</i></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, and the other photo is from the current timeline, an example of Istros' Knife (from </span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Tome of the Pentacle</i></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\">). The players might be seeing through the rewrites because they were also Shielded (since Jacob was keeping an eye on them), with the timeline inconsistencies triggering the Mystery Play. </span></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T10:39:49-08:00","id":1554975,"title":"","content":"They say go big or go home, and you certainly went big with these theories, haha. I love it.<br /> <br /> Congratulations, you've earned yourself an NPC named after you! There was one element of your guess that unambiguously hit the mark. I think I'm gonna leave which major element that you sussed out a mystery of its own for now, though. The answer might actually surprise you.<br /> <br /> With only three chapters left in Story 0, you're all about to receive a lot of answers about what's going on and even more questions. If anyone's got any other theories or questions you'd like me to answer, send them my way. I guarantee you nothing gives your local Storyteller more of a dopamine hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T13:15:07-08:00","id":1555073,"title":"","content":"Wow, I read a bit so far and looks great!! So far really well written and with lots of good ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28905-keeperofthedarkhound","name":"KeeperoftheDarkHound","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28905_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T14:53:45-08:00","id":1555074,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Glad to have you along for the ride.<br /> <br /> I was going to post the next writeup tomorrow, but I might just upload it later tonight instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T19:48:50-08:00","id":1555089,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2bcc 0.3 | Down the Rabbit Hole</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">\u201cWho in the world am I? Ah, that's the great puzzle.\u201d \u2014 Lewis Carroll, Alice in Wonderland</span></div> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\">\u2bcc \u2bce \u2bcc</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">This session was shorter than usual because of scheduling issues. Despite that, and the fact that the entire session takes place within the same building, there's a lot of information gained and foreshadowing of future events. This\u2019ll be a fun one to look back on in future stories. Keep your hard hats on, everybody, because the twists and turns are only just beginning!</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Sam Bishop stands behind a car in a parking garage, sucking on a chocolate Tootsie Pop with a phone pressed to his ear. He doesn't bother to introduce himself as the call connects.<br /> <br /> &quot;Cover's been blown\u2014I was forced to interfere.&quot;<br /> <br /> He quickly corrects himself.<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, perhaps forced to is not quite accurate. But I made a snap judgment, and it was my call to make. I don't micromanage you, so lay off a bit, huh?&quot;<br /> <br /> He seems to take in the voice on the other end, thinking.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, speaking of jobs,\u201d he says, voice muffled by the candy in his mouth, \u201chere's how this is going to go down. After I hang up, you're going to dial the last number in your call history. I imagine you can handle the rest on your own.&quot; He pulls off the Tootsie Pop with a wet pop and loudly crunches down on it.<br /> <br /> &quot;There, that better?&quot;<br /> <br /> The voice on the other end is silent.<br /> <br /> &quot;Cheer up, I've got eyes on her right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> In the trunk lies a woman, unmoving, limbs and hair splayed in every direction.<br /> <br /> Sam slams it shut and gets down to business.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">Switching perspectives at the beginning of the session here was something I did more or less on a whim, but players responded really well to it. And so, from this point onward, it\u2019s become an Echo Chamber tradition to start with the camera somewhere else (and occasionally end that way too). My players are great about not metagaming using the information their characters don\u2019t know, and it gives them a chance to see what the NPCs get up to when the PCs aren't around. In that way, it\u2019s both a tool for generating intrigue and something that makes the world feel fuller and more alive.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Damian gets a call from Oliver asking if he knows where Sarah is. He doesn't; the last time heard from her was this morning on the way to the funeral. Ollie says he talked to her just before her lunch break, which she has a habit of taking early, around 11:30. But he figures that she might be off with Damian's \u201cfriend.\u201d This immediately raises some warning flags for Damian, who does not have any friends who would have a reason to interact with his staff in any capacity. He grows increasingly more concerned when Ollie shares his texts with Sarah, who was visited in the office by this \u201cfriend\u201d who claimed he and Damian went way back. Damian makes a note to check in on Sarah when he's done with this weirdness at UCLA.<br /> <br /> Collin, listening in on the conversation, gets incredibly nervous and decides to give Dave a call for good measure. After four long rings, the call connects.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, Dave, um\u2026 question. Has your internet or phone service been really spotty recently... since being out here?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> All he hears on the other end is the sound of cars whooshing by.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Are you safe, Dave?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> He checks the Find My App and discovers that Dave has turned off location sharing.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Dave, I don't know if you can hear me, but I cannot hear you. All I can hear is cars. If you can hear me, message me when you can, okay bud? Stay safe, please.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Collin freaks out after hanging up, and Damian is curious about the app he was using to track Dave. Being an elderly man (read: millennial in his late 30s), he has no clue about newfangled technologies like that. Unfortunately, he\u2019s not the kind of guy who has the funds for an iPhone, and even if he did Sarah probably wouldn\u2019t share her location with him 24/7. As they talk, Damian hears the sound of footsteps approaching and recognizes a few voices. He turns the corner and sees The Gothip Girls (and their ordinary-looking third wheel) from the funeral arguing amongst themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"372\" height=\"481\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/QvQTtuB.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/QvQTtuB.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/QvQTtuB.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Ugh. I can't believe how bad my luck is. What are the chances Elias would be on break right now?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"372\" height=\"481\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/FOPhlEP.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/FOPhlEP.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/FOPhlEP.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Well, if Emily hadn't taken so long...&quot;<br /> <br /> Emily, the odd one out in terms of both personality and appearance, decides she doesn\u2019t want to be a part of the conversation and excuses herself, staying behind as the other two round the corner. None of them notice Damian surreptitiously eavesdropping on their conversation as he hangs out by the bulletin board. Meanwhile, Collin is looking into potential service outages in the area and why someone might not show up on the Find My app. He finds some generic advice about removing devices from settings and reinstalling, doing factory resets after backing up data, and other things he classifies as \u201cbullshit.\u201d But he does see a recent post in the UCLA subreddit from an hour ago entitled &quot;What is up with the signal around the quad today?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">Did you consider that maybe Dave just doesn\u2019t want to be around you right now, Collin?</span><br /> <br /> Seeing the girls around the corner, he immediately recognizes them and accosts the leader.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh. Oh! You were at the funeral, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> She seems taken aback by the out of the blue question from a stranger. When she asks if he\u2019s a student here (since she doesn\u2019t recognize him and the graduate program is rather small), he says yes\u2026 but online. Then he asks her about her cell service and whether it\u2019s been spotty at all today.<br /> <br /> &quot;No, it's fine, creepy dude.... It says I've got like, 5 bars.&quot;<br /> <br /> When he tells her that he was friends with Jacob, it\u2019s like a flip has switched within her. She goes over to him and tries to hold his hand (though he instinctively flinches away from the contact), saying that Jacob was a joy to be in class with. He was a star student, and apparently was well-liked, if her reaction is anything to go by. Collin figures that since she was a friend and classmate, she\u2019d be the perfect person to give him some answers and pulls out the medallion he found in Jacob\u2019s room earlier.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you recognize this?\u201d<br /> <br /> Before he even realizes what\u2019s going on, she lunges for the medallion, trying to tear it from his grasp. Fortunately, Collin is able to keep it out of her reach, and he decides to slip it back inside his shirt where she won\u2019t be able to get it so easily. He shouts to Damian for help as she calls him a thief and demands he return it. When Damian rounds the corner and asks for an explanation, the girl says Collin has stolen something that doesn't belong to him. Collin responds by accusing her of being the one trying to steal something.<br /> <br /> Damian points out that the medallion technically belongs to Mrs. Carver, and since they\u2019re her representatives here, it only makes sense for them to have it. Seeing that arguing is futile, Gothip Girl #1 dials a number, puts the phone to her ear, and runs off. Her satellite raises her hands in surrender and follows behind.<br /> <br /> Given all the drama the medallion has caused thus far, Damian and Collin figure it\u2019s best to put it someplace safe. The back window of Damian\u2019s Chevy Cruise is cracked open, so he asks Collin to head back and put the unlucky trinket inside. In the meantime, he heads around the corner and finds the third wheel of the Gothip Girls standing around with earbuds in, listening to music and apparently unaware of the squabble that just occurred. He approaches and tries to get her attention. Surprisingly, she seems to recognize him.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, you were in the back with that guy who totally ate shit.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">If you remember, Derrik nearly split his skull in two trying to climb backward over a pew at the church.</span><br /> <br /> She tells him about the odd little club that Deeanne, the queen bee of their little clique, is a member of. According to her it\u2019s a weird Greek Life-esque situation funded by alumni of the school. Members wear togas during celebrations and speak in Latin, and they call themselves the Legion, though she\u2019s sure they refer to themselves as something else that she can\u2019t recall. Deeanne is a \u201cCenturion,\u201d which appears to be a middle-ranked leadership position.<br /> <br /> &quot;Weren't you talking to Abigail at the funeral? I think she'd be the person to talk to. It is her club, after all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Damian can tell she\u2019s holding something back, and though she\u2019s a little tight-lipped at first, not wanting to gossip about the others lest she inadvertently become a pariah, Damian doesn\u2019t have to try very hard to get her to spill the beans. She seems to be fairly miffed with the others, and grumbles about Deeanne deciding to go to the funeral at all when she hated Jacob. Apparently they were enemies, but it was completely one-sided. Emily figures that Deeanne\u2019s reason for attending was Elias, her former TA who she\u2019s \u201cdown bad for.\u201d Unfortunately (or maybe fortunately), he didn\u2019t show up to the funeral.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Back in Elias\u2019s office, the man of the hour tells Ray and Derrik to make themselves comfortable, \u201cthough it seems like you already have.\u201d He says that people have been barging into his office all day, but hopefully with the door locked they\u2019ll have to at least knock first next time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"372\" height=\"481\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/ZRpXVkB.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/ZRpXVkB.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/ZRpXVkB.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;So, are you the temps... or?&quot;<br /> <br /> Derrik gives a noncommittal answer, not denying it but not actually saying they are either. Elias doesn\u2019t seem to notice and asks if they want tea. Derrik seems about to refuse when Ray mentions that he\u2019d love some. Elias turns to his cabinet, pulls out some mugs, and begins to get to work. Meanwhile, Derrik is looking at Ray in panic, as if to say, What are we supposed to do now? Ray just shrugs back, looking equally out of sorts.<br /> <br /> Elias asks how much they know about what the requirements are for the temp job. Derrik continues to be as vague as possible with his response, asking Elias to assume they haven\u2019t been appropriately briefed on the responsibilities. The other man sighs and grumbles about the lack of preparedness despite all the funding that the department gets.<br /> <br /> Regardless, he gives Derrik and Ray the broad strokes of the situation. The original professor for their course on mythology and magic had a medical emergency at the beginning of the year and is still on leave. As such, it fell to the TAs to do everything, and they are woefully understaffed. He needs temps to collect assignments, field emails, and proctor the final exam if possible. When he asks if either of them have any experience with anthropology, Ray says he took a course when he was in undergrad, and Derrik says it wasn\u2019t part of the department, but yes.<br /> <br /> As Elias sets down the tea, Derrik notices the steam wafting from the surface reshape itself into odd geometric patterns and can\u2019t tear his eyes away from it. Ray hands over syllabi for the course and asks the two of them to familiarize themselves with it, saying he\u2019ll get them the student list later. He gives them a sticky pad to jot down their numbers, and asks them their names, writing them on the sticky pad above their numbers. Surprisingly, he spells Derrik Thorpe right on the first try, without any assistance.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think that's the first person I've ever seen do that right aside from family members\u2026&quot;<br /> <br /> Elias shrugs and says that people spell his name wrong all the time, too, adding a W to Ren.<br /> <br /> &quot;I suppose I'm good at guessing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Outside, Collin looks around as he slips the medallion through a crack in the window. But as his fingers make contact with the glass, it shatters. A burning sensation wells up in his fingers as they start to bleed. All around him, silver butterflies hover in the air, seemingly drawn toward his bleeding fingers. Upon closer inspection, their wings appear to be completely metallic, their antenna and legs made out of segments of tiny silver arrows placed end to end like segments without any visible joints. Each of the butterflies seems to be sporting an elaborate silver eye mask, like they\u2019re set to attend a masquerade. They land on his bloody fingers before taking off in another direction.<br /> <br /> Collin looks away for a brief moment to find something to wipe his hand, but when he looks back he\u2019s no longer in the parking lot and nothing is as he remembers it. In front of him rests an ornate silver chariot with crimson accents. It is dark out, nighttime, with a large crescent moon glittering in the sky. All around there are chariots in various designs, all made of the same glimmering silver. Wildgrass grows freely from the ground, along with bushes laden with black roses. The butterflies from before have landed on the front bumper of one particular chariot across from what was once Damian\u2019s car. This one was rimmed wheels with a spiky and rather modern look to them. The butterflies stop their flapping as he approaches, turning to him.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hello.&quot;<br /> <br /> A series of high-pitched giggles echo around him as the butterflies shatter one by one, splattering the surface of the chariot crimson. There is the sound of straining metal as what was once the bumper of a car dents and twists as if subjected to unimaginable force.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">Screwy: Oh no, this is going to be Dave!</span><br /> <br /> Panic rises in his chest, but despite it all Collin manages to tamp it down.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">7 Successes!</span><br /> <br /> The eerie giggles fade as mist rolls out in all directions. As Collin turns to look back, what was once the UCLA Anthropology building is now a set of massive doors to the large grandfather clock he remembers from his dream. It towers above him, reaching up into the sky. Unfortunately, he\u2019s unable to see the clock face. reaching up into the sky. More silver mist flows from the open doors to the clock, and a cloud of butterflies float inside, the sound of giggling accompanying them.<br /> <br /> When he enters, he finds the interior of the building exactly how he left it aside from the mist billowing from around the distant corner and the butterflies that seem insistent on taking him somewhere. Damian cannot see any of that but notices a silvery mist or aura of some kind wrapped around Collin\u2019s head, seeming to move along with him. He reaches out and tries to swat at it, causing Collin to hear the sound of glass shattering and tell him to stop. Without much explanation, Collin heads further down the hallway, eager to follow the butterflies to his destination.<br /> <br /> Damian is suddenly overcome by a sensation of vertigo despite being very firmly planted on steady, stable ground. When he blinks, every surface around him is mirrored. For some reason, Collin doesn\u2019t seem to reflect in any of them, but he does\u2014in every single surface. Hundreds, maybe thousands of Damians stand in a seemingly endless sea of recursive reflections of reflections, each of them looking at him with a different expression on their faces. The air smells slightly of sulphur.<br /> <br /> Like any sane man in this situation, Damian immediately goes for his cigarettes, but he can\u2019t find them. What\u2019s more, as he looks down he notices a metal plate on his chest, with a round dial on one side. The metal is bent in places, damaged, with scratches and gouges marring the surface. What\u2019s more, this metal plate seems to be protruding directly from his chest like the door to a safe. He hears the sound of rattling metal and notes heavy metal cuffs on each of his wrists, the chains connected to the outer edges of the safe door where a group of other chains are attached. Each is a different shape, thickness, and size. Most look painfully sharp, covered in barbs, hooks, and in one case, razor wire. What those chains connect to is impossible to tell, as they hang down low on the floor, stretching out all the way down the corridor in both directions and around the corners and out of sight.<br /> <br /> Continuing to follow behind Collin, Damian digs his fingers into the underside of the safe door, trying to see if he can pry open the door. Oddly, he doesn\u2019t feel flesh or his ribs underneath, just empty space. Still, he continues to tug, wanting to get the thing out of his chest. As he does, the hall fills with the sound of creaking of metal and the myriad reflections around him have crowded in close, their hands pressed up against the reflective surfaces, palms stained red., feels like he could rip this open if he put his back into it. All the reflections around him have crowded in close, their hands pressed up against the reflective surfaces, hands stained red. Finally, the metal door gives and he tears it open, but his sense of satisfaction is short-lived as he sees the swirling black void in his chest and another wave of vertigo overtakes him. An overpowering pressure begins to build in his neck as he feels his body being pulled toward the epicenter, his neck bending at an unnatural angle as he crumples inward on himself, sucked into the void he unleashed.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s back in the hallway, braced against a wall and freed of that awful vertigo. His cigarettes and lighters are splayed out on the floor, and the only sign that anything weird had even happened is the faint but inescapable smell of smoke and brimstone.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">I\u2019m very happy with how this scene turned out. As I\u2019ve mentioned a little before, my philosophy leans toward \u201cDon\u2019t prep plots,\u201d or as I prefer to call it, \u201csituations over scripts.\u201d Though this entire session took place in the Anthropology building and there was a set of characters I knew were inside, none of what you\u2019ve seen so far (aside from the opening and closing scenes) was scripted. Even the trippy weirdness Collin and Damian just experienced was off the cuff and a result of the actions they\u2019d taken. I honestly hadn\u2019t expected them to fight with the Gothip girls or drop their fancy Key Item in an unattended car, but boy am I enjoying the aftermath of it! There\u2019s almost nothing I love more than putting player characters in a situation and seeing what they decide to do about it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">Also, can I just say that Collian and Damian\u2019s reactions to the trippy weirdness they\u2019re experiencing are hilarious to me? Neither of them have stopped to process what\u2019s going on, much less suggested to each other that weirdness is afoot. The onward march toward the goal cannot be stopped. But even so, the energy they\u2019re bringing with them is different. Collin is giving small stepchild from a cruel European fairytale following enchanting creatures into the jaws of danger, whereas Damian is giving, \u201cThe mirror dimension torture chamber hallucination again? Huh, I guess it is Tuesday\u2026 Man, I need a drink.\u201d</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> &quot;Is there anything else you need from me?&quot; Elias asks after he\u2019s collected their contact information.<br /> <br /> Derrik makes a comment about Elias being invited to the funeral. He flinches, saying there were no invitations as far as he's aware, and asks why the two of them were at the funeral if they\u2019re not part of the Anthropology department. Ray pipes up that he was there for work.<br /> <br /> By way of response, Derrik hands over his polaroid and the invitation, running his fingers over the embossing. When he sees the name on the kids\u2019 shirts, Elias mentions that there\u2019s an unincorporated community in California named Whispering Pines. Apparently they had a set of cabins or a resort of some kind that burned down in the California fires some 10 odd years ago.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">It\u2019s a real location, about 7 hours north of Los Angeles by car. A family-owned cabin retreat since the early 1930s, regularly rented out for group events and camps and such. Funny enough, Keni was the one who came up with the name of this South Dakota faith camp. I was extremely amused when I first saw it in Derrik\u2019s backstory. I love a happy coincidence.</span><br /> <br /> After a pause, Derrik begins to ask a question he\u2019s been wondering ever since he saw that Elias was the screensaver for Jacob\u2019s laptop.<br /> <br /> &quot;Were you two...?&quot;<br /> <br /> Elias slowly sips his tea.<br /> <br /> He says that Jacob was a bright, motivated student who was always fascinated and curious about the content. He showed up for every set of office hours and was a model student in the class.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe was a wonderful person, I'm sure. It's a shame.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sorry,\u201d Derrik replies somewhat coyly, \u201cI thought you guys were closer.&quot;<br /> <br /> When Elias says that he\u2019s got no clue why he\u2019d come to that conclusion, Derrik says that he\u2019s seen pictures of Elias taken by Jacob. There is a palpable shift in the energy of the room as Elias tenses up in his seat.<br /> <br /> &quot;That's hard to imagine. He's not really the type to take pictures.&quot;<br /> <br /> Derrik bursts out laughing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">Au contraire, Mr. Teaching Assistant. He had polaroid pictures, ID photo pictures, webcam pictures, grainy camera pictures\u2026 Seems like he was an equal opportunity picture taker.</span><br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not sure what to say. I can't particularly confirm or deny what one of my former students did.&quot;<br /> <br /> He admits that some of the students in his class were a little &quot;much&quot; in that department. Deeanne, in particular, can be very clingy, he says. Given that, it's not totally surprising to hear that a student might do something like that.<br /> <br /> Ray suddenly turns around as if he's noticed something, but then turns back and shakes his head.<br /> <br /> Seeing the Jacob conversation has led nowhere, Derrik confirms that they're going to be getting the schedule and student list.<br /> <br /> &quot;It would be quite a misstep if I forgot to send my temps the schedule and the roster of students... but you're not really here to be my temps are you, Derrik?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">Keni\u2019s deer in the headlights expression was wonderful.</span><br /> <br /> &quot;What makes you say that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, for starters, you're not a student at this school. You graduated, was it\u2026 2 years ago, I believe? From the Law School?&quot;<br /> <br /> Derrik sets his jaw.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're a lawyer\u2014&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;\u2014Not Yet.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A soon to be lawyer, and you live in the Hollywood area, correct?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Why do you know where I live, Elias?&quot;<br /> <br /> Elias slaps the polaroid of Whispering Pines on the table facing Derrik.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, I imagine the reason I know where you live is the same reason you have the strange idea that Jacob has a picture of me as one of his screensavers. Probably because this picture was in his room.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...This was in his room?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, you didn't know that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Nope,&quot; Derrik says, smirking.<br /> <br /> Elias says that once he learned about Jacob\u2019s situation, he\u2019d told him how absolutely mental it all was. But Jacob didn\u2019t seem interested in listening to what he had to say.<br /> <br /> &quot;But he did have a lot to say about you and... who 