;Dontlookdontlookdontlook.&quot;</i></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Collin follows the butterflies through a maze of corridors before they finally reach their destination: a massive door with intricate silver filigree. Elias\u2019s name is carved into the surface of the door in an intricate cursive script and inlaid with gemstones. According to the clock on the door, he should be returning anytime soon. As Collin watches it, he realizes that the clock uses a decorative silver arrow, engraved with patterns and symbols, instead of an hour hand.<br /> <br /> An array of strange symbols that call to mind those from the medallion carve themselves into the frame of the door, starting from the bottom and slowly climbing on either side and meeting at the center. As they reach the top and the entire frame is filled, a silvery crescent moon appears facedown above the door, lasting only a few moments before it fades out and the carved runes fill themselves in from the top of the door to the bottom, as if they were never even there to begin with.<br /> <br /> The cloud of butterflies around Collin moves toward the door and melts into it, disappearing from view.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Damian grabs his cigarettes from the floor, the slightest physical contact enough to make him feel a little better.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">Addiction is a hell of a thing.</span><br /> <br /> As he follows behind Collin, Damian takes note of the fact that he\u2019s expertly navigating the corridors without any guide or reference, never hesitating or looking back. He\u2019s never been here, but it\u2019s as if he\u2019s navigating his way through his house rather than an unfamiliar, labyrinthine building. For some reason he can\u2019t imagine, Collin stops in front of a plain wooden door, staring at it in wonderment and awe.<br /> <br /> When Collin knocks on the locked door, he feels a familiar burning sensation as the arrow is dislodged from the clock, falling to the floor. Its tip is stained crimson, and the entire thing is oddly warm to the touch. To Damian\u2019s eyes, Collin swats at the plastic hand on one of the cheap time in/time out clocks on the door, knocks it to the ground, and then examines it as if he\u2019s staring at the Hope diamond.<br /> <br /> &quot;Colln, what are you doing?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;This arrow is warm.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">He\u2019s never beating the allegations.</span><br /> <br /> Collin's blood seems to sink into the grooves that are carved along the surface of the arrow, running from point to end, causing the fletching to shift from a rainbow starburst pattern to a bright crimson. Damian, naturally, does not witness any of this. He notes the name on the door and Collin's odd behavior over the past several minutes.<br /> <br /> &quot;I thought you didn't know where he was?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Where who was?&quot;<br /> <br /> Exasperated, Damian decides it best to ignore him and knocks loudly on the door, at which point he hears the rattling of metal and swears he can see a metal cuff around his wrist. Some of the chains hanging from it trail all the way to the ground and through the gap under the door.<br /> <br /> Back in Elias's office, Ray sniffs a couple times and turns to look at the door, murmuring that he thinks Damian is on the way. Derrik, incredulous, asks if he just sniffed the air to identify a person. Ray simply says that it smells like cancer and cologne, but all Derrik can smell is lavender.<br /> <br /> He makes the mistake of glancing at the candle, at which point the hum of a choir picks up in the background, hundreds of perfect voices harmonizing.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Nononononono.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> When they hear the knock at the door, Ray excitedly announces that it's Collin and Damian. Derrik rises to his feet to let them in, though halfway through he realizes he\u2019ll have to look in the direction of the blackboard and so decides to 