ng at Elias. And though none of the PCs see it, the other man is glaring daggers at him the entire time.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> On the outside, Collin is entranced by the arrow and the intricate designs carved along its surface. He wants to cover it in ink and roll it on a piece of paper to see what kinds of patterns it makes, but doesn't have any ink on him. So he does the only reasonable thing in this situation and cuts himself with it, coating it in his blood, and then rolls it along the (now blank) paper he got from Elias's office. When he does, two strange things occur: First, the imprint left on the paper is silver rather than red. Second, and somehow even stranger, the imprint of the arrow on the paper creates an almost replica of the map of Union Station that they found on Jacob's murder wall. It's almost a replica because the one difference is a faint, hair-like line forming a tunnel in the vague shape of the number 5 that he\u2019s certain was not there on the other map. Collin excitedly shows Derrik the map and arrow, explaining how he used his own blood as ink. Much to Derrik's horror, he can see a glowing golden outline around them.<br /> <br /> &quot;Maybe you should put that away and NEVER show anyone again.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just then, the others exit Elias's office and Derrik tries to push the map and arrow away from himself and hide them, accidentally jabbing the arrow into Collin's chest. It hurts, but thankfully, his lucky silver handkerchief, folded up in his coat pocket, provides just enough padding to prevent any actual damage. To nobody\u2019s surprise, Collin immediately rushes to show Damian and Ray the map, ignoring the universal SHUT UP signal that Derrik is trying to send him.<br /> <br /> &quot;So what I did was\u2014&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Stop talking. STOP TALKING.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What is going on?&quot; Damian asks, concerned about whatever this is.<br /> <br /> &quot;He's being weird,&quot; Collin explains matter-of-factly.<br /> <br /> &quot;He's just saying the things that he normally does that aren't gonna make any sense.&quot;<br /> <br /> Collin bristles at that. &quot;How does this not make any sense? I put my blood on the arrow, rolled it on the paper, and it made a map of friggin' Union Station!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;COLLIN, YOU CAN SEE THINGS OTHER PEOPLE CAN'T SEE. <span style=\"color:#E74C3C\">SHUT THE FUCK UP!!!!</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Every light along the hallway simultaneously shatters, plunging the entire area into darkness as glass rain downs on everyone's heads. Damian immediately reaches for his lighter, and with the faint light that the flame projects, it is easy to see that they are no longer in the Anthropology building. In fact, right behind him Damian catches sight of a sign pointing to the train line below.<br /> <br /> As he does, their sole source of light flickers, sputtering for but a moment before dying out.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> In his office, Elias reaches down and opens a drawer, shuffling its contents around and finally withdrawing a set of keys on a square ring. One of them is made of heavy iron in the shape of a skull, sapphires glittering where its eyes would be. He puts it down on the desk, pulls out a phone and makes a call, placing it against his ear. He doesn't wait for an answer as the person on the other end picks up, instead delivering a single line and then hanging up.<br /> <br /> &quot;They were here.&quot;<br /> <br /> With that he grabs the keys, throws them in his satchel, and makes a mad dash for the door of his office. He throws it open behind him as he flees the Anthropology building, not bothering to bring anything else with him.<br /> <br /> The hallway outside his office is completely empty.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">I really enjoyed this session even though it was a good hour shorter than I\u2019d have liked it to be. There were a lot of good character moments, we finally learned a bit about Derrik\u2019s backstory and aversion to church, we got to see some really weird stuff happen with the boys, and Elias\u2019s place in the mystery becomes clear\u2026 and then less so by the end.<br /> <br /> As always, if you\u2019ve got any comments, burning questions, or theories, feel free to throw them my way.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":28942,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","user":"synchrosanct","date":". 11-04-2025, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T14:20:53-08:00","id":1555177,"title":"","content":"Elias and Ray seem to be playing a high stakes game. I really love the glimpses from other character\u2019s point of view.<br /> <br /> Are you using the expanded details on Awakenings from <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> ? Because if so, it's may mean both are taking huge risks by involving themselves in the Mystery Plays, both mystical and social, especially since becoming part of the Mystery Play does not guarantee your safety.<br /> <br /> The slow burn leading towards Awakening is done really well. The characters potray being in their own kind of obsessive satori. The gradual escalation of symbolism, weirdness and of the unexplained phenomena is pretty cool to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T10:52:30-08:00","id":1555364,"title":"","content":"Glad you're having fun with the alternate POVs. Plenty more where those came from.<br /> <br /> Absolutely, I love Chapter 6 of SoS! The only thing I'm tweaking significantly is the sublimation process for pneuma, since it goes away too fast in my opinion. Instead I'm making it so that your pattern fills with pneuma, giving you the normal benefits up to your mana capacity. So newly-Awakened mages would have 10 uses of pneuma, but a higher Gnosis mage, especially those Gnosis 7 and above, get significantly more mileage out of it. This also has the rider effect of making the monitoring of the Lucid and competing for the title of Mentor an even more tense and serious affair. Less scrupulous (and somewhat reckless) mages might try and use you as a pneuma battery, while the average Adept might just swoop in to try and Mentor you (and have you use your pneuma for their benefit, since it's likely to last into the first few weeks of your training).<br /> <br /> The next writeup, which should be coming either sometime today or tomorrow, will touch a little bit on the dangers of intruding on a Mystery Play. As for the political consequences, those will feature heavily in the next story.<br /> <br /> Really happy that it's being well received! I wasn't sure how it would all end up playing out, but the slow-burn approach was the right move imo. There's so much gold in an Awakening scenario, and going through it fundamentally changes you as a person (as Temporal Sympathy shows), so not getting to explore that in a regular game is a shame. I'm really excited to see what you think about the trials they go through soon.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T02:05:45-08:00","id":1555428,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2bcc</span> </b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>0.4 | Wake Up</b></span><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"center\">\u201cDo you wake up as I do, having forgotten what it is that hurts or where, until you move? There is a second of consciousness that is clean again. A second that is you, without memory or experience, the animal warm and waking into a brand new world. There is the sun dissolving the dark, and light as clear as music, filling the room where you sleep and the other rooms behind your eyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2014 Jeanette Winterson<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2bcc \u2bce \u2bcc</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">We are approaching the point of no return for our unlikely trio. Despite the strangeness of the circumstances they\u2019ve found themselves in, the obstacles and antagonistic forces both mundane and horrific, and their own perceptions betraying them, they have not given in to the desire to look the other way or run. No, despite it all they\u2019ve dared to pursue this mystery to its conclusion, to find the answers at the heart of the mystery of Jacob Carver.<br /> <br /> <br /> I can't believe we only have one writeup left for Waking World Dream after this. Things start taking a distinct turn for the weird, even compared to the strange things we\u2019ve seen thus far. Will they be able to handle it or will they crack under the pressure, their minds and souls unable to handle the Truth? And what happens when forces beyond their comprehension meddle with their investigation, causing things to spiral out of control? Keep reading to find out!</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Dave pulls over. He turns to his passenger, apologizing for the traffic. The other man tells him it\u2019s definitely no problem; this is what LA is like. Suddenly, his phone rings. The Caller ID says COLLIN.<br /> <br /> <br /> He frowns at it, looking... uncertain.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;... You gonna take that?&quot; the man sitting in the passenger seat asks.<br /> <br /> <br /> It continues to ring.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;You're right, I probably should,&quot; he says as it rings a fourth time, taking a shaky breath before hitting Accept.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Dave!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Hey boss,&quot; Dave says, looking over at his passenger, who gives him a reassuring thumbs up. &quot;What's up?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Oh goodness, thank you, I was worried. So uh, when\u2014 I'm not back at, uh, we're not back at the church. We're actually over here at the university. I was trying to find where you were because your phone\u2014&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> His voice is drowned out by two ambulances driving by, sirens blaring loudly in the background.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;What's going on?&quot; Collin squeaks out, pitch rising in concern.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dave begins to respond, but as his words cross over to the other side they're staticky and garbled and Collin cannot make them out. The call drops.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">If you remember from two sessions ago, Collin tried and failed to properly contact Dave when they got to Jacob\u2019s room. This is the other side of that conversation. But who exactly is Dave with? Why is he so nervous to pick up the phone? And what became of him after this point?</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> A woman with almost white-blonde hair and striking blue eyes stands tall in a smart blazer paired with a colorful buttoned blouse and a shark skirt. The judge stares down at her from his seat.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Please rise.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> She does so with an effortless grace, clearly at home in the tense court environment. But there's a tightness in her jaw as she listens to his next words. &quot;Elaine Thorpe, on the aforementioned charges of aggravated assault, espionage, perjury, and murder in the first degree, how do you plead?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> She lifts a golden cross to her lips and kisses it before opening her mouth to speak.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Guilty, your honor.&quot;<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Sarah awakens with a start to find her vision completely dark.<br /> <br /> <br /> It\u2019s hot and humid and claustrophobic, and she realizes that there\u2019s something over her head. When she tries to open her mouth to speak, she realizes that it\u2019s been taped shut. Her hands are bound behind her, her legs tied to the plastic chair she\u2019s sitting in.<br /> <br /> <br /> Muffled by the bag over her head, she can hear faint footsteps approaching before the burlap sack is torn from off her head. She stares up at the figure in front of her, eyes widening as they speak.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cHello Sarah, would you like to play a game?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">This time we have a three for one with the starting scenes!</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> The area the characters have found themselves in is dry and dusty and smells of rust. The ground is somewhat uneven under them as they stumble around in the darkness. Damian can hear the slow drip of liquid, feeling the ripples of something wet underfoot with each step. Collin cannot escape the sound of crunching glass that accompanies every footfall. Derrick, on the other hand, hears the low hum of electricity in the background and sees his companions as golden outlines in the shape of people, moving through the otherwise pitch-black environment. He\u2019s able to distinguish them primarily from the fact that Damian\u2019s outline extends to his lighter. In the faint glow of these coronas, he spots thousands of golden irises staring at him in unison as they begin to sing in chorus.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Hey Damian, what's in your hand?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Just a lighter\u2026?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah. How about you use it right now?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Though it seemed ineffective before, Damian concentrates and flicks his lighter open. It sparks to life, changing the flame\u2019s hue shifting through a chromatic scale as Damian\u2019s entire hand erupts in prismatic flames that don't seem to burn or give off any heat whatsoever. Despite this, the surface of the lighter burns away, turning a near jet black as runes appear all across its surface. To Derrik, this all appears as an explosion of light that is blinding. As the last of the lighter burns up, the flames dissolve into sparks that fall to the ground and light it up like an oil slick. Tongues of multicolored flame cascade outwards, ripples burning away the environment to reveal the corridor they were in before. There is no glass on the floor, no damage to the building, and no nameplate on Elia\u2019s door, which is ajar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">Every time they try and redefine the world around them in contradiction of what they see and feel, I have them roll their Integrity. Xeno happened to roll 5 successes on this one.<br /> <br /> Xeno: I'm integrated as shit.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Derrik, looking around, realizes that he can\u2019t find Ray anywhere.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Somewhere else, Ray stumbles around in the dark, blinking in confusion. Not understanding how he got there, he calls out a greeting and it echoes back to him, the pitch and timbre of his voice distorting each time the word returns. He reaches for his phone, but it seems to be missing. Far off in the distance, he seems to catch sight of something and approaches, footsteps echoing behind him. The strange acoustics make it seem like there are several pairs of footsteps trailing just behind him. He spots something far off in the distance, and as he gets closer, he seems to catch sight of a series of words. Briefly, his eyes widen\u2014first in shock, then realization, and finally horror. They bulge, wider, and wider and a bead of red forms at one corner of each eye, trailing its way down to his chin before dropping and splattering on the ground. He doesn't react, transfixed, as, without warning, the drops become trickles of blood, then spurts, until finally a veritable torrent of blood pours from his eyes as he stands still, transfixed in horror, mouth hanging open even as it fills with blood from the fountain pouring from his eyes. Then, all of a sudden, the torrent stops and he tips over backwards, eyes glazed over, making a loud splash in the sea of blood underfoot as he sinks beneath the surface.<br /> <br /> <br /> He does not reemerge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">The players made a joke the previous session about Ray being the government-assigned DMPC for the group and it took all my willpower not to laugh like a hyena.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Collin notes that Elias\u2019s office no longer seems like an office, heading inside. The entire place is barren aside from a blackboard in the center. While it looks to be new, closer inspection reveals miniscule striation patterns on the surface, nearly imperceptible to the naked eye. The more he stares, the more patterns begin to form in them. At first, he sees the number 5. But then he realizes it\u2019s actually more of a G. And the lines on the surface next to it seem to form an O.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#E74C3C\">GO.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Derrick, meanwhile, is getting increasingly worried about Ray. He pulls out his phone to call him but notices that the last number he dialed was his mother\u2019s. And other than his therapist, it looks like he didn\u2019t make any other calls today. He calls Ray\u2019s number to mind, though it feels oddly fuzzy in his memory. Regardless, he\u2019s able to power through the mental block and remember the sequence of numbers. When he goes to input them, he realizes they\u2019re already typed in for him.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Stop doing that, please.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The battery dies, much to his chagrin.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I don't know, turn back on?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> It does, and he and the other two each get a ping as text messages come in. They\u2019re all from the same unfamiliar number and contain a photo of security camera footage from what appears to be a train station. At this point, they can all recognize it as being Union Station. In the picture, 5 individuals are standing around one another. Though they\u2019re wearing different clothing, it\u2019s obviously the three of them engaged in a conversation, with a fourth figure standing with their back to the camera. They\u2019re a little shorter than him, dress like a young person, with a vaguely dorito-shaped build. Derrik notices a leg in the corner, as if a fifth person had walked out of frame. With the poor resolution, it\u2019s hard to tell precisely, but they\u2019re wearing sneakers and have some sort of black band or tattoo of some sort above their ankle. Opening the thumbnail further, Collin realizes that it\u2019s a picture of a screen, and makes out the reflection of a timestamp reading August 1st, 11:00 p.m. It only takes a moment for him to recall that Jacob was discovered on the morning of the 2nd and thus likely died on the night of the 1st.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cDidn\u2019t they find the kid around this time?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Derrik has a strong reaction to that.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cUsed to be your friend, now calling him \u2018kid\u2019?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">Derrik Thorpe, Shadow Name: Hypocritus.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> The lights in the building all shut off at once, eliminating all illumination aside from the pale blue light filtering in through the window. It\u2019s 10:00 p.m. at this point\u2014somehow nearly 5 hours have passed since they left Elias's office. Unable to make sense of it, they make plans to head to Union Station to get to the bottom of the mystery, though Damian's worry about Sarah is more pressing. He offers to give both Collin and Derrik a ride.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m very concerned about Dave, my\u2026.. my\u2026 the guy who brought me here. But there\u2019s nothing I can do about it right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Derrik asks for confirmation yet again of whether Dave is actually his boyfriend, but Collin firmly denies it. What ensues is a conversation about what exactly a &quot;personal concierge&quot; is, since the others think of guys who work at hotels and not\u2026 whatever it is they have going on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">Honestly, I can\u2019t blame Derrik for being stuck on that train of thought. It really does seem like that\u2019s what Collin\u2019s implying, but I know there\u2019s no romantic intent there whatsoever. That\u2019s just his emotional support guy.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cThink about a modern day butler, but not a butler. He\u2019s a friend but I trust him with my life.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;He's a friend but you pay him?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Well, I guess that works out,\u201d Damian cuts in. \u201cBut in any case, can we get the hell out of this school?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Derrik briefly stops to look out the window and feels like something just moved away as he approached the sill. On the ground outside the window are two footprints depressed into the grass of the lawn, outlined in gold. A light vapor, as if from fading heat, rises from the ground. As he rushes to shut the window, the first few notes of a 12 part harmony start up around him.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Nothing there!&quot; Derrik says a little too loudly, voice cracking.<br /> <br /> <br /> After making their way to the parking lot, they find Damian's car, back window broken and glass fragments strewn across the asphalt. Damian looks to Collin's hands and sees they're red, as if covered in blood. They struggle briefly as he grabs them and Collin tries to avoid physical contact, but there's no escaping his vice grip. To Damian, Collin's palms bear no injuries but appear a glossy red, casting a distorted version of his face in their reflection. To Collin, his hands look completely normal, though the lines on his palms do seem to make a vague &quot;5&quot; shape when he focuses on them. Derrik takes his phone out and starts recording this altercation for posterity.<br /> <br /> <br /> A cursory search of the car reveals that the medallion is gone, and oddly enough, there isn't any glass on the inside of the car. It's almost as if the windows shattered outwards. But with much more pressing concerns, the trio hop in the car and make their way out of Westwood.<br /> <br /> <br /> As they make their way to Damian's apartment, Derrik tries and fails to call Ray, only getting an automated voice that says the number is not in service. For some reason, there\u2019s a distorted echo to the last few words before the call drops. Damian, meanwhile, is listening to the police scanner and catches chatter about a girl in her 20s reported missing in the vicinity of downtown near Union Station, as well as a pack of African painted dogs and maned wolves that escaped from the zoo.<br /> <br /> <br /> At that precise moment, Collin gets a notification about cellular congestion in the area leading to his service being temporarily limited. As he's exiting out of the notification, he catches sight of a news article sharing facts about African Painted Dogs. This sets him off immediately and he messages Steve.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Collin: I'm getting targeted auditory ads.<br /> <br /> Steve: No you're not, dude.<br /> <br /> Collin: Yes. Something over the radio I've never researched just gave me a popup suggestion.<br /> <br /> Steve: Uhh... I don't know that targeted ads happen that fast. </div> </div> </div><br /> Collin proceeds down to dive headfirst down the African painted dog rabbit hole and is generally unresponsive for the next hour or two. When they arrive at Damian's apartment, Derrik follows him inside. It reeks of cigarettes and booze, and the puddle on the floor from when he woke up this morning is still there and just as sticky. Damian checks his messages for updates on Sarah, learning that she apparently shared a story a couple hours ago near a train station, and prints out the picture of the Minotaur from earlier before sticking it on his very own murder well. Finally, he gets out his .44 caliber revolver, equips his gun harness, and gets ready to do business. Sam Spadey, his guinea pig, puts his little paw up to the inside of the enclosure as the two turn to leave, completely missing the figure who emerges from Damian's bedroom momentarily before returning inside.<br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Collin is learning cool animal facts. It turns out African painted dogs' scientific name is lycaon pictus, which means &quot;painted wolf.&quot; Oddly enough, African painted dogs are neither dogs nor wolves (both being members of the genus Canis), but rather the only surviving member of the genus Lycaon. They are highly social pack animals with an alpha pair, whose pups all the other members of the pack raise communally, their own breeding functions suppressed. They are also one of the only species that actively care for the sick, elderly, and dying rather than abandoning them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">I ran this rabbit hole research project as an Extended Action Wits + Computer test. It was fun to throw a bunch of trivia about African painted dogs at Screwy. They're fascinating animals that can actually be found at the Los Angeles Zoo. Or rather, they could be found at the Los Angeles Zoo. I\u2019ve just robbed you of the opportunity to see them for yourself.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Strangely, when looking at the letters of the genus, Lycaon, they take on a silvery sheen on the screen. He taps the word and it pops up the various options: Select, Select All, Copy, Search the Web.<br /> <br /> <br /> Derrik follows Damian into his office, focused on texting his therapist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Derrik: We can talk, does it have to be in person? </div> </div> </div><br /> He turns off his location sharing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Therapist: Yes.<br /> <br /> Derrik: Are you at the office now???<br /> <br /> Therapist: I\u2019ll be there when you get there.<br /> <br /> Derrik: That doesn\u2019t make sense at all.<br /> <br /> Therapist: I\u2019ll explain in person. </div> </div> </div><br /> Damian turns on Sarah\u2019s computer and checks the low-quality security cam footage. Somebody wearing a trenchcoat and a fancy fedora walked in around 11:30, just before Sarah\u2019s usual break. The brim of his hat covers the top half of his face but reveals the scraggly beard of someone who hasn\u2019t shaved in some time. His hair is dark, either brown or black. Rewinding, he sees Sarah get a call, showing remarkable interest in the conversation. This strikes him as unusual, as she\u2019s only really shown interest in the current case of a dog stolen from a micro-influencer that Ollie is working on. Rather than leave at 11:30, she hangs around, at which point the man enters and talks to her for a few minutes. Then he leaves. She says something to herself, types on her phone, then turns everything off and heads off for her lunch break, never returning. Though he can\u2019t place it, the man in the recording feels very familiar to Damian.<br /> <br /> <br /> The old TV in the office is still on, repeating an earlier news segment discussing the influx of a new invasive species of beetles, with entomologists weighing in on what it means in the context of climate change. Damian turns it off and coordinates the next leg of their journey with Derrik.<br /> <br /> <br /> While this is happening, the door opposite Cal opens up and Sam Bishop climbs in, startling Cal.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cWhere have you been?\u201d he asks the older man.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cYou have no idea how busy I\u2019ve been today,\u201d Sam replies, pulling out a chocolate Tootsie Pop.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cWant one?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cYou know, against my better judgment\u2026 Normally I would say no thank you, but it has been a day and I would love one please and thank you.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> As Collin unfurls it, he notices some strange things about the wrapping. The children on the front have masks covering their eyes and instead of a star pattern there\u2019s just a grandfather clock-like shape. On the inside of the wrapper, there\u2019s silvery writing asking how many licks it takes to get to the center of a Tootsie Pop.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cI never made it without biting. Ask Mr. Owl.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> But his joke lands on deaf ears, as the car is empty.<br /> <br /> <br /> The door suddenly opens and Derrik enters, resulting in an argument about whether or not Collin actually saw Sam. When Derrik ignores him, he turns his attention back to the task at hand and begins counting. It\u2019s a lot easier than he expected, though, because after 5 licks he reaches the core\u2014a perfectly spherical ball of silver metal.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just then, the channel on the radio randomly switches, and the DJ says they\u2019re playing some of Maroon 5\u2019s greatest hits, including Not Coming Home, Wakeup Call, It Was Always You, Last Chance, Must Get Out, and Echo. Derrik quickly switches to something else, saying that he hates how whiny they are.<br /> <br /> <br /> Soon enough, they arrive at Derrik\u2019s apartment and Damian pulls into the space next to his green Astin Martin despite Derrik\u2019s request not to. They leave Collin in the backseat once again, but not before Derrik takes another potshot at him.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cI think I know why the guy you hired is your only friend.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Derrik\u2019s electricity is back on, but the clocks aren\u2019t set. He quickly changes out of his formal clothes and looks for his regular phone, but can\u2019t find it. Looking under his bed, there are no signs of anything aside from a couple of small blood spatters. Using his flashlight, he can\u2019t seem to find any source of the blood. The bottom side of his mattress looks just fine. So he gives up after a cursory check of the room yields no phone or anything else of note.<br /> <br /> <br /> He and the therapist make plans to meet tomorrow instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> Emerging from his room, Damian can see a few of Derrik\u2019s tattoos for the first time. There are lots of leaves, near his elbow and a zipper pattern on his right wrist, along with a thorny somewhat tribal-looking tattoo crawling up his neck on the left side.<br /> <br /> <br /> Damian tries to smoke but is ushered out by Derrik, causing them both to miss Brian Williams lying in the bathtub in a pool of his own blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> Outside, Collin is on a roll and has no intentions of stopping. He\u2019s learned that the genus of the African painted dogs is named after a Greek king named Lycaon who purportedly tested the omniscience of Zeus by cooking his son in a feast dedicated to the king of the gods. According to one retelling of the story, Zeus brought his son back to life and instead cursed the father to become a wolf. In other versions of the story, he learns, Lycaon is said to be a father of a nymph named Callisto who pledged herself to Artemis but was tricked into sleeping with Zeus and becoming pregnant with his child. Some versions say she was cursed for breaking her vow of chastity and turned into a bear by Artemis. Arcus, her son and later king, comes across her bear form and nearly kills her. Zeus, perhaps taking pity on them, raises them both up and places them in the sky to form Ursa Major and Ursa Minor. In another retelling, Hera, enraged by her husband\u2019s infidelity, demands that Artemis slay her own maiden. In that version of the story, Artemis takes her silver bow and arrow to slay the bear, but Zeus again turns it into a constellation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">I love the classic Greek myths as much as the next person, but there\u2019s an entire goldmine of more obscure ones out there and I was excited to be able to share this one with Screwy to reward Collin\u2019s dedication to the deep dive. We\u2019ll definitely be coming back to this myth again and again in the chronicle.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Collin cannot help but feel an iIntense sense of nostalgia about this story, learning that the land was named Arcadia after Callisto\u2019s son Arcus. Seeing the word causes flashes of color and light to overwhelm his vision as he\u2019s hit with overwhelming twinned sensations of deja vu and inevitability. It\u2019s as if, in that moment, he\u2019s standing at the edge of the shore watching a tsunami about to come crashing down on him. When Derrik and Damian get back in the car, he jumps, startled out of his thousand yard stare.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cYou see Sam again?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Collin says no, he was just thinking, but doesn\u2019t bother to elaborate. He doesn\u2019t know how he\u2019d even explain all of that. But luckily, he doesn\u2019t have to, because Derrik says he wants to introduce them all to a \u201cvery fun game.\u201d He holds out his wrist with the zipper tattoo showing and says that if he messes with it, it\u2019s a warning sign to keep quiet because someone might be listening. The more Collin stares at the zipper, the more realistic it seems, until he watches it peel back, the top portion of Derrik\u2019s wrist popping off as silvery threads wrap around him, Damian, and Collin before tightening around them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Collin looks back at the wrapper, which is now blank. But the silver ball he\u2019s rolling between his fingers bears a distinctive set of grooves on its surface. Together, they make the number 5.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, Dave, um question.. has your internet or phone service been really spotty recently... since being out here?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Cars whoosh by on the highway.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Are you safe, Dave?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The figure on the other end of the call looks at his wristwatch counting down: 5, 4, 3, 2, 1\u2026 Then he opens up the Find My app and disables his location sharing.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Daaave...!&quot; Collin pleads, to no avail.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Dave I don't know if you can hear me, but I cannot hear you, all I can hear is cars. If you can hear me, message me when you can, okay bud? Stay safe.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The man in his finely tailored blue suit slips Dave\u2019s phone into his pocket and walks off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">Screwy: Wait, where\u2019s Dave? Where\u2019s my buddy?</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> At long last, they arrive at Union station, a massive structure in the Spanish Revival and Art Deco styles with huge arches and a large rectangular prism clocktower with a design for its face. On the inside it bears massive vaulted ceilings, frescos, and numerous paintings. It\u2019s past 11:00 p.m., close to midnight, and there are no cars nearby. Damian announces that the first stop is Baggage Services.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oddly enough, the front doors to the station are not locked. The corridor on the inside, however, is completely dark. He lets in the other two, and Derrik is immediately on the lookout for security cameras. Luckily, they don\u2019t seem to be turned on. Damian pulls out his flashlight, Derrik uses his phone\u2019s light, and between the two of them they have more than enough illumination to navigate. But places look very different at night, especially in the dark with only the intense beams of flashlights to guide them. Shadows move ever so slightly, and everything looks bigger and more foreboding under the harsh lighting.<br /> <br /> <br /> For some reason, the lights are on in Baggage Services. Damian shushes everyone with a hand gesture and tries to sneak closer, only to miss a puddle of something slick on the ground, slip, and thump against the wall loudly. As he trains his flashlight on the ground, he knows, somehow, that it\u2019s a dark purple, almost black viscous liquid, but when the light illuminates it all he sees is oil.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cThis place is going to shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Having lost the element of surprise, he casually walks into the office. A young man in his early 20s in a visor listens to music through wired earbuds and pops his pink bubble gum loudly. Damian approaches and hands over the stub from Jacob\u2019s murder well to the guy in charge, whose nametag reads RUDY.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just outside, Derrick is playing with shadows on the wall using his phone\u2019s flashlight. Collin, meanwhile, is focused on the frescoes. The ceiling mosaic directly above him depicts an archer shooting an arrow into the sky, which explodes outward into a starburst pattern. He can identify Ursa Major in the sky, but there is no Ursa Minor to go along with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cSo, how\u2019s your day been so far?\u201d Rudy asks.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s been\u2026 wild.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cGnarly! I\u2019ve had a pretty wild day too, man.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cOh yeah. How so?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Rudy just says that it\u2019s crazy the things that people will just leave behind. He squints at the stub, looks back up at Damian, and mentions being familiar with this one. Space 125 has been reserved for quite some time, though he notes that Damian is not the usual guy. Damian simply says he\u2019s picking it up for a friend.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rudy says that Jacob didn\u2019t really seem like he had a lot of friends, but that\u2019s \u201cgood on you, man.\u201d He heads back into the storage area, popping his gum and humming along to the music playing from the one earbud he still has in. Damian takes the opportunity to do a quick visual scan of the area while Rudy\u2019s not at the desk, but it doesn\u2019t turn up anything too unusual. The most notable thing is that the computer terminal right in front of him does not seem to be powered on at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> After a few minutes, Rudy returns.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry, man. Looks like one of Jacob's other friends must have come by and picked it up earlier.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Damian asks if they gave a name, and Rudy goes to the powered off computer and starts typing. After a few moments of that, he apologizes and says there\u2019s no hits. But he does mention that Jacob\u2019s pickups are usually at 8:00 pm or so at night, followed by dropoffs the following morning at 8:00 a.m. That\u2019s a pattern that has remained true for the past few weeks, though Rudy says he hasn\u2019t seen Jacob in a few days at this point. Amtrak has a policy of not storing things for very long, but seeing as how Jacob is a regular, Rudy looked the other way. Continuing to type away at the keyboard, Rudy says that maybe he can find a note somewhere. Not too long later, he says there was a man with a long coat and a fancy hat.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cYou know what? I think I know him.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> When Damian asks him for the stub back, Rudy tilts his head and asks him what he\u2019s talking about, the smile never leaving his face. Damian narrows his eyes, giving him a dry \u201cReally?\u201d before he leaves out the front door, maintaining eye contact the entire time. Rudy just waves until long after he\u2019s out of sight. Then, the lights turn off and the doors are locked from the inside.<br /> <br /> <br /> As the three of them discuss the marked lack of a package, they all hear footsteps coming from the direction of the front doors they just came through. the direction they came from. All they can make out at first is the bottom of a trenchcoat as a person wearing boots walks around a corner, heading back the way they came. Derrik is distracted by the sound of harmonizing voices in the background, but Damian gives chase. As he makes his way into a long hallway, he sees the man in the trenchcoat pushing open a series of doors that lead into the dark. The man turns to look over his shoulder for the briefest of moments, showing a slight glimpse of his side profile, and Damian immediately recognizes the face of one Jayce Henry.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cJay\u2014HOLD IT!\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> The figure smirks and takes off into the dark, the area on the other side of the door so covered in shadow that the light of Damian\u2019s flashlight will not pierce it. He charges in and the other two follow behind, everyone arriving in a long, dark tunnel that smells of rust, dust, and an almost imperceptible cloyingly sweet smell. The floors and walls are covered in grime as far as the eye can see. None of them can hear footsteps in the distance, but they all swear they can see the silhouette of a person all the way at the other end of the corridor. It looks like whoever they are, this person is shorter than Jayce and decidedly not dorito-shaped either.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cDid you see Jayce?\u201d Derrik asks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Jayce?<br /> <br /> <br /> Jayce?<br /> <br /> <br /> Jayce.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">J\u0335\u0343\u0322a\u0337\u030e\u0347y\u0337\u0310\u0348c\u0335\u0314\u0324e\u0335\u0304\u0332?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cOh no, fuck that. I\u2019m out.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> But there is no exit. Only a dark corner that the light of his phone refuses to penetrate. In this moment, Collin is once again hit by that same sense of deja vu and inevitability from earlier. The silhouette from the other end of the corridor seems to vanish without any trace or sound, and against his better judgment, Derrik tries to do something a little unorthodox. He closes his eyes, focuses his thoughts, and tries to search for the \u201cleft behind essence\u201d of that person, reasoning it might be similar to the gold-outlined footprints from before. All at once, the walls begin to bend and expand, revealing intricate fractal patterns carved into gold walls beneath the grime. All around him he can see small halos that shoot off into the distance across the length of the corridor.<br /> <br /> <br /> When Derrik catches sight of the beam of light coming from Damian\u2019s flashlight, he can see every individual particle that forms that beam broken down to its smallest component\u2014but what he sees are not particles, but rather glowing ball-like angels, rings covered in countless eyes that seem to be singing in chorus, excited at the fact that he\u2019s finally acknowledging their presence. Collin hears the sound of crunching glass underfoot with each step he takes. The walls on either side of him become covered with brambles and thorns, but never the portion ahead, always just spots at the periphery of his vision. When he looks directly at them, they\u2019re no longer there. Damian, instead, hears the sound of menacing laughter and smells smoke and something noxious in the air.<br /> <br /> <br /> After a bit more walking, the three of them see a tiny pinprick of light at the very end of the hallway. The sensations they\u2019re experiencing become more intense with each step. Derrik can see waves rippling from every movement of their bodies, see the heat radiating off of them. Collin catches sight of silvery motes in the air and silver butterflies that flutter about in droves making tinkling noises. Every step he takes leaves crushed glass and silver underneath his feet. Damian feels the jingling of chains as the safe door returns to its rightful place on his chest. This time, he can see that he\u2019s connected to Derrik and Collin, feeling the pressure build behind his eyes as he follows the other set of chains that seem to extend much further into the dark.<br /> <br /> <br /> Collin has his eyes closed and he\u2019s rubbing the silver core of the Tootsie Pop while covering his ears to try and ignore the sound of crunching glass and silver. At some point, he realizes he hasn\u2019t felt the 5 shape made by the grooves in quite some time. When he looks, his hand is completely empty. But rolling toward him from the end of the corridor is a silver ball that comes to a stop just underneath the toe of his shoe. He stops, crouches, and after freaking out about how unsanitary it is, picks it up and holds it in his palm. He cleans it off with wet wipes and spots his distorted reflection across its surface. The ball rolls from his palm up toward his finger, seeming to move in defiance of gravity. He feels like he\u2019s dreamed about something really similar to this recently.<br /> <br /> <br /> Collin flips his hand, kneels down, and places the silver ball on the ground right in front of his shoe. Then he stands back up, looking at the ball in surprise in confusion as it rolls back toward the end of the corridor at incredible speed.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Protect them.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Protect them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Protect them?<br /> <br /> <br /> Protect them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">P\u0334r\u0338o\u0337t\u0337e\u0338c\u0335t\u0334 \u0337t\u0338h\u0336e\u0337m\u0336.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> As they reach the end of the tunnel, it opens up into a strange space. There are no walls, floors, or ceilings\u2014it\u2019s just pitch black in every conceivable direction. But it's impossible to focus on that because the sight they see ahead of them is a truly massive set of gates that towers over everything else, dwarfing even the clocktower they saw outside. As far as they can tell, there are no walls or floors\u2014the gate is not anchored to anything that they can see, and even though the space behind the gate is completely black like the rest of this place, all three of them feel like they can sense something else just beyond. Parts of the gate bear barbs and chains, others floral designs, some geometric shapes, and other portions seem to be bent and twisted unnaturally.<br /> <br /> <br /> A lone figure stands in front of the gate, a ring of keys in his hands. Despite the lack of ambient light in the area, the sapphire eyes set into the iron skull of the key seem to glimmer as he places it into a tiny keyhole on the towering gate. There is a soft click.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I can't let them do this.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Let them do this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do this?<br /> <br /> <br /> Do this.<br /> <br /> <br /> This.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">T\u0335\u0350\u0356h\u0338\u030a\u032di\u0334\u0304\u0332s\u0335\u030f\u035a.\u0337\u0310\u0333</span><br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cI have to stop them.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Stop them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Stop them?<br /> <br /> <br /> Stop them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">S\u0336\u0343\u033a\u0349\u034e\u0327t\u0336\u0352\u0314\u0307\u0312\u0305\u0357\u0359\u0331\u035a\u0320\u0333o\u0337\u0358\u035d\u0314\u0342\u0331\u0326\u0348p\u0334\u0315\u031f\u032e \u0334\u030b\u032e\u033ct\u0335\u0307\u0344\u0340\u031a\u0319h\u0335\u030d\u0303\u0340\u035d\u0353\u0348\u031f\u0359\u034d\u0348e\u0334\u0301\u0312\u0351\u0316\u0328\u0331\u031e\u032f\u0348m\u0337\u0357\u0357\u034a\u0302\u0313\u033b</span><br /> <br /> <br /> The echoes reverberate louder and louder in the dark space, becoming more and more distorted as they reach their peak, sounding like unintelligible whispers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Damian runs toward the gate, followed from behind by Collin, who sees the silver ball roll under the legs of the figure ahead, under the gate, and then vanishing. Damian runs toward the figure, feels a strange sensation as if the ground keeps expanding below his feet. The figure in front of him gets smaller and smaller and smaller as if moving further away, even though the gate stays the same size. Then things flip and the figure becomes bigger and bigger as the ground contracts between them, until eventually Damian is stuck looking up at this person looming above him. He was originally planning on grabbing the keys, but instead he slows down to try and figure out what exactly is going on. The trippy sensation ends and he dashes forward, ripping the keys from the other person\u2019s grip.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I have to start them.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Start them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Start them?<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">S\u0335\u0341\u0327t\u0334\u0300\u0349a\u0337\u0346\u0327r\u0338\u0312\u0327t\u0338\u0315\u0330 \u0337\u035d\u0329t\u0337\u0301\u0321h\u0334\u0305\u0332e\u0336\u0301\u033am\u0335\u0306\u032c</span><br /> <br /> <br /> The bars of the gate seem to melt away into the shadows as the area behind the gate is suddenly illuminated with a pulsing white light. Derrik, Damian, and Colline experience a sensation like the world being flipped upside down and then grabbed by a pair of hands, twisted, and ripped apart. An overwhelming wrongness suffuses everything, their lungs and hearts gripped in a vice by cold hands as the light behind the gate turns blood red.<br /> <br /> <br /> The figure takes a step back, clearly surprised, and turns around. For the briefest of moments, bathed in the red light from behind the gate, the three of them can make out some of the details. He's wearing some sort of jacket made from a solid, inflexible material\u2014maybe denim. His hair is dark, slightly wavy and tousled, and a pair of sunglasses lay on top of his head, glowing blood red from the light passing through them from behind.<br /> <br /> <br /> But where his face should be, they all see a flat surface like a mirror, lined with cracks. In each segment, bathed in this red light, they see different features from different faces, arranged like an incorrect jigsaw puzzle. Together, they form a sort of patchwork collage of a face whose individual parts don\u2019t go together, each cracked sliver shifting erratically, shifting from one feature to another faster than any of them can process what the entire face looks like together. Damian, who is closest, gets the distinct impression that the guy in front of him is trying to say something but it\u2019s impossible, as the various fragments that make up his mouth shift constantly, making it impossible to read his lips. Somehow, they all feel as if time has slowed to a complete stop in this chamber.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regardless of how many times the slivers shift, they can all feel abject horror radiating from each fragment as a dark liquid begins to pool in the cracks. The constantly shifting amalgam of mouth parts open as if to speak, and finally manages to get out two words.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#E74C3C\">W\u0335\u030f\u0314\u0353\u0321\u0326a\u0334\u034a\u0330\u0317\u032b\u0321k\u0334\u0342\u031a\u0313\u034b\u0314\u0342\u034e\u0347\u0317\u0330\u0348\u033b\u0345e\u0334\u035d\u035d\u0346\u0357\u0313\u030c\u031b\u035c\u033c\u032a\u031d\u0355\u0353\u0329 \u0337\u0346\u0303\u0315\u031a\u0356\u032e\u034d\u035a\u0356\u031f\u0347\u0318\u035cu\u0337\u0357\u0344\u035c\u033ap\u0336\u034b\u0303\u030d\u034c\u030c\u030e\u034e.\u0335\u030f\u0350\u0302\u0344\u0305\u034d\u0326\u0323\u0339\u032e</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Without warning, the face fragments explode in a flurry of glass and blood, traveling far further than they have any right to. Damian feels millions of tiny shards dig into his skin, innumerable points of fire as he is knocked off his feet and thrown to the ground. As he lands hard on his back, the three of them see a veritable tidal wave of blood rising up taller than the gate itself ever did before crashing down upon them.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1ABC9C\">I\u2019m really satisfied with how this one turned out. There was a nice buildup over the course of the episode, culminating in some really freaky (and sad) moments at the very end. Screwy summed it up pretty well immediately after we ended the session.<br /> <br /> <br /> Screwy: What the fuck are we getting into, man?<br /> <br /> <br /> What indeed, what indeed.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":28942,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","user":"synchrosanct","date":". 11-13-2025, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T15:42:18-08:00","id":1555440,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They went from an approaching moment of cosmic epiphany to experiencing cosmic horror, and they almost went <i>Through The Gate of the Silver Key</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> All things considered, I theorize the players got the best outcome. I think The Gate tried to make them experience a Tyrannical Awakening when they were in the crossing the Abyss phase of the Mystery Play, and it almost managed it too. But since Damian remembered to get the Keys, it experienced a moment of shock (since I imagine the Exarch of Paradox's words and actions contradict themselves). When it lost some ability to regulate the Abyss, it decided to abort before the players were called to the Ziggurats.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it means that their Awakening failed, which will lead to some very though Breaking Point rolls, plus lots of consequences to them and the Defilers who tricked them into getting the Keys. However, this might be a blessing for Derrik, he is so afraid of the Aether that I suspect he has a high chance of experiencing a Harrowing Awakening with his current mindset. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Some very intriguing developments, I am looking forward to reading what happens next.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T18:05:44-08:00","id":1555696,"title":"","content":"Derrik Thorpe's player, Keni, here poking my head in.<br /> <br /> synchrosanct is cool with me lurking here and it's a pleasure to read every update as I love our game so much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28974-kenishra","name":"Kenishra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28974_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T12:44:15-08:00","id":1555734,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-\u2bce-the-echo-chamber-\u2bce-2e-actual-play?p=1555440#post1555440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They went from an approaching moment of cosmic epiphany to experiencing cosmic horror, and they almost went <i>Through The Gate of the Silver Key</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> All things considered, I theorize the players got the best outcome. I think The Gate tried to make them experience a Tyrannical Awakening when they were in the crossing the Abyss phase of the Mystery Play, and it almost managed it too. But since Damian remembered to get the Keys, it experienced a moment of shock (since I imagine the Exarch of Paradox's words and actions contradict themselves). When it lost some ability to regulate the Abyss, it decided to abort before the players were called to the Ziggurats.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it means that their Awakening failed, which will lead to some very though Breaking Point rolls, plus lots of consequences to them and the Defilers who tricked them into getting the Keys. However, this might be a blessing for Derrik, he is so afraid of the Aether that I suspect he has a high chance of experiencing a Harrowing Awakening with his current mindset. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Some very intriguing developments, I am looking forward to reading what happens next.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Almost <i>Through The Gate of the Silver Key</i>, indeed.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I agree, they made the best of a <i>very</i> bad situation. I'm a very &quot;let the chips fall where they may&quot; Storyteller, so I was fully prepared to explore bad routes if certain choices were made or others were avoided. I love your thoughts on the Gate and feel quite similarly! An Eleventh Exarch, a supposed Supernal symbol of absolute tyranny, of order and control, who does not represent an Arcanum like the others but the Abyss itself, all that is unordered and chaotic and cannot and should not be. Just the words &quot;regulate the Abyss&quot; are madness, much less the actual fulfillment of that duty. If the Gate's not a walking contradiction, I don't know what is!<br /> <br /> If you couldn't already tell, The Gate is by far my favorite Exarch, though The Father gets honorary mention for smiting those who go digging into the past for evidence of Jesus Christ's existence and for the fraught relationship he has with his Minister.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I also wanted to mention that Keni and I were talking about you the other day and how you always have such great comments about the story. I did share one of your theories (the very last sentence about Derrik in your spoiler) with them since we've progressed far enough in the story at this point that they know exactly what all those terms mean and why it's such a big problem. You're 100% correct about that!<br /> <br /> Also, speak of the devil! Welcome to the thread, Keni.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the delay in posting the final installment of Waking World Dream. It should be coming sometime this weekend, likely tomorrow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554737-%E2%AF%8E-the-echo-chamber-%E2%AF%8E-2e-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">\u2bce The Echo Chamber \u2bce</span></b> <span style=\"color:#1abc9c\">[Mage: The Awakening 2e Actual Play]</span> </a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28942-synchrosanct","name":"synchrosanct","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28942_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T16:22:15-08:00","id":1555866,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thank you, the chronicle has been so fascinating so far that I cannot help but speculate. I'm glad that theory was right, and that Derrik dodged that bullet.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Those are great picks, the Gate has such strong flavor and potential plot hooks. </div></div> </div> </div></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Do not worship the Gate, for you do not want the frontier of unreality to be metaphysically closer to the world. </span><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A living contradiction at it's core, with it's own liminal space in the Place Between. The Secret Order of the Gate are like Lovecraftian cultists, walking the tight rope between the horrors of the Exarchs and the madness of the Abyss, all the while fearing becoming Scelestus and being paranoid of having some infiltrating their ranks. Their actions also represent an eldritch Mystery for players to uncover. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Since the Gate was created after the Celestial Ladder collapsed, it leaves the story of their Ascension open to speculation, as the Exarchs had to <a href=\"https://youtu.be/DlXJuvGQfA4?si=mMbL5vmSkMrkGJzi\" target=\"_blank\">find a candidate and perform a ritual</a>. Maybe the ritual was paradoxical, and they had to lose their name to gain their title, maybe it embodied itself and that is where Marduk came from. It leaves interesting open Mysteries as plot hooks.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Father also was the one who turned an Arrow when he vanished for a &quot;audience with the divine&quot;, and whatever emerged that looked like Veritas went on to create the first Seer Ministry.<br /> </span></div></div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <br /> <br /> <i>Observation: </i>For some reason it broke it into two spoiler tags, and I am not sure why.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}